(339, 'Five', 'Description The 5th day of the 5th month in the 5th year of the century. Shoot anything relating to the number 5.', '2005-05-05', '2005-05-06', '2005-05-07', '2005-05-13', 182, 2, 35774, 1776, 5.269, 7.387, 5.23, 3.683),
(340, 'Silhouettes II', 'Description Silhouettes are created by backlit subjects, which causes them to appear solid and without much detail. Submit your best silhouette taken this week!', '2005-05-09', '2005-05-15', '2005-05-16', '2005-05-22', 248, 3, 58137, 2858, 5.392, 7.722, 5.3298, 3.437),
(341, 'Apple', 'Description Take an apple (the fruit, not a computer!) anywhere, do anything you like to it, but make the shot your own.', '2005-05-11', '2005-05-17', '2005-05-18', '2005-05-24', 386, 10, 118359, 4682, 5.175, 7.491, 5.1742, 2.956),
(342, 'Lighting II', 'Description Lighting is arguably the most important element in photography. Without light, you can''t capture an image. Use lighting in a creative fashion this week so that the lighting itself is a key factor in your composition.', '2005-05-16', '2005-05-22', '2005-05-23', '2005-05-29', 239, 5, 48421, 2107, 5.395, 7.47, 5.4024, 3.558),
(343, 'Granular', 'Description Take a photograph in which your subject is granular, such as powder, sand, salt or dust.', '2005-05-18', '2005-05-24', '2005-05-25', '2005-05-31', 327, 6, 91877, 3548, 5.102, 7.212, 5.0946, 2.318),
(344, 'Beauty', 'Description Beauty is very hard to describe, but we all know it when we see it. Take a photo that makes the viewer say "that''s beautiful."', '2005-05-23', '2005-05-29', '2005-05-30', '2005-06-05', 255, 1, 64040, 2724, 5.435, 7.302, 5.4153, 3.283),
(345, 'Decisions', 'Description We all have to make them. Creatively shoot a decision.', '2005-05-25', '2005-05-31', '2005-06-01', '2005-06-07', 275, 2, 82021, 3585, 4.916, 6.64, 4.9136, 2.738),
(346, 'Naturally Framed', 'Description Take a photograph where the subject is naturally framed in by its surroundings.', '2005-05-30', '2005-06-05', '2005-06-06', '2005-06-12', 223, 0, 49535, 2241, 5.399, 7.675, 5.3736, 3.856),
(347, 'Construction', 'Description Road construction, building construction, housing construction. Construction is everywhere. Usually it''s not a pretty sight. Your challenge, difficult as it may be, is to create, compose and shoot an artistic rendition of something construction oriented.', '2005-06-01', '2005-06-07', '2005-06-08', '2005-06-14', 305, 10, 88307, 3310, 5.074, 7.225, 5.05045, 2.485),
(348, 'Birds', 'Description Take a picture where one or more birds are the main subject.', '2005-06-06', '2005-06-12', '2005-06-13', '2005-06-19', 289, 2, 76357, 4046, 5.488, 7.638, 5.50295, 3.034),
(349, 'Darkness', 'Description What does darkness mean to you? Show us with an image.', '2005-06-08', '2005-06-14', '2005-06-15', '2005-06-21', 373, 11, 112995, 4640, 5.03, 6.898, 4.9902, 3.248),
(350, 'Fantasy World', 'Description Photograph something that you might see in a world beyond our own.', '2005-06-13', '2005-06-19', '2005-06-20', '2005-06-26', 151, 8, 32015, 1969, 5.389, 6.962, 5.3303, 3.558),
(351, 'Metal', 'Description If it''s made of metal (you know, usually shiny, good conductor of heat and electricity), you can photograph it for this challenge. Whatever metal object(s) you use should be the primary subject. There is a lot of metal in the world, so the key here is being creative. Good luck!', '2005-06-15', '2005-06-21', '2005-06-22', '2005-06-28', 508, 13, 139419, 5729, 5.084, 7.888, 5.1149, 2.603),
(352, 'Leading Lines II', 'Description Use this compositional technique to deliver the impact of your photograph.', '2005-06-20', '2005-06-26', '2005-06-27', '2005-07-03', 275, 3, 65463, 3799, 5.432, 7.745, 5.3927, 3.444),
(353, 'Obsolete', 'Description Take a picture of something that has outlived its usefulness. It could be old technology, broken, discarded, outgrown, forgotten - anything. Exception: people (alive or dead) are not to be the main subject.', '2005-06-22', '2005-06-28', '2005-06-29', '2005-07-05', 453, 11, 119855, 4735, 4.974, 6.759, 4.9658, 2.759),
(354, 'Macro V', 'Description It''s been a while! Get up close and personal with the subject of your choice. You need not specifically use your macro feature, but your image should be a close-up shot.', '2005-06-27', '2005-07-03', '2005-07-04', '2005-07-10', 374, 5, 90604, 5338, 5.409, 7.796, 5.3804, 2.458),
(355, 'Circle', 'Description Take a photograph where this basic shape is clearly shown as a key element. This may be a circular object, or a group of items forming a circle.', '2005-06-29', '2005-07-05', '2005-07-06', '2005-07-12', 545, 12, 156185, 6351, 4.954, 7.23, 4.9397, 3.046),
(356, 'Family', 'Description Take a photograph that conveys the idea of family. Your photo need not contain a person.', '2005-07-04', '2005-07-10', '2005-07-11', '2005-07-17', 159, 3, 38869, 3378, 5.295, 7.0, 5.2505, 3.642),
(357, 'Sports II', 'Description Capture the action of the sport of your choice.', '2005-07-06', '2005-07-12', '2005-07-13', '2005-07-19', 296, 7, 100604, 4257, 5.134, 7.505, 5.06285, 2.29),
(358, 'Independence', 'Description N/A', '2005-07-10', '2005-07-16', '2005-07-17', '2005-07-23', 139, 1, 29347, 1591, 5.422, 7.099, 5.3828, 3.231),
(359, 'At the Zoo', 'Description Take a photograph of something you might see at a zoo.', '2005-07-11', '2005-07-17', '2005-07-18', '2005-07-24', 198, 0, 45060, 2188, 5.622, 7.524, 5.704, 3.712),
(360, 'Textures III', 'Description A texture occurs in a photograph because of the interaction between light and a three dimensional surface. Use this information to make the viewer "feel" the appearance of your subject.', '2005-07-13', '2005-07-19', '2005-07-20', '2005-07-26', 614, 7, 166203, 5156, 5.1237, 7.2509, 5.093, 2.6945),
(361, 'Wooden', 'Description Wood is cut and dried and used as raw material for many things. Your challenge is to capture a photograph where "wood" is an important component of the composition. Creativity is key!', '2005-07-18', '2005-07-24', '2005-07-25', '2005-07-31', 251, 0, 46408, 2341, 5.296, 7.137, 5.2033, 2.716),
(362, 'Tools of the Trade', 'Description Photograph the tools specific to a certain trade/job, i.e. camera and film, hammer and nails, needle and scalpel.', '2005-07-20', '2005-07-26', '2005-07-27', '2005-08-02', 342, 5, 92481, 3747, 4.99237, 7.0326, 5.0038, 2.7336),
(363, 'Long Exposure', 'Description Long exposures can often create very dramatic effects in photography. Use a longer than normal exposure to create the impact of your image.', '2005-07-25', '2005-07-31', '2005-08-01', '2005-08-07', 200, 0, 47709, 2422, 5.441, 7.524, 5.3859, 3.665),
(364, 'Affluence', 'Description The opposite of the poverty challenge. Knock us out with your representation of material wealth.', '2005-07-27', '2005-08-02', '2005-08-03', '2005-08-09', 232, 8, 66826, 2949, 4.92256, 6.4194, 4.93675, 2.0),
(365, 'Room', 'Description To celebrate DPC Fanatics (the unofficial chatroom)''s 3rd birthday, take a photo of your interpretation of the word ''room''. Be creative!', '2005-07-29', '2005-07-29', '2005-07-30', '2005-08-05', 138, 2, 29993, 1803, 5.282, 7.397, 5.2466, 3.682),
(366, 'Illusions II', 'Description Things are not always as they seem. Set up an illusion to trick your viewers.', '2005-08-01', '2005-08-07', '2005-08-08', '2005-08-14', 127, 6, 34761, 3950, 5.497, 7.391, 5.41585, 3.642),
(367, 'Time Capsule', 'Description Take a shot that depicts an era in time. Your title should be the year that you are trying to capture for future generations.', '2005-08-03', '2005-08-09', '2005-08-10', '2005-08-16', 298, 7, 83942, 3980, 5.142, 7.493, 5.108, 3.521),
(368, 'Rain', 'Description Be careful with your equipment this week as you search out your best photo of rain.', '2005-08-08', '2005-08-14', '2005-08-15', '2005-08-21', 228, 1, 67692, 3764, 5.4, 7.527, 5.299, 3.524),
(369, 'Live Music', 'Description To coincide with the get-out-and-shoot member challenge on monday (Rain), find some live music to photograph. Good luck!', '2005-08-10', '2005-08-16', '2005-08-17', '2005-08-23', 210, 9, 72190, 3800, 5.172, 7.084, 5.1949, 2.397),
(370, 'Nude III', 'Description It''s time once again to try out this popular style of photography. As always, keep it tasteful.', '2005-08-15', '2005-08-21', '2005-08-22', '2005-08-28', 118, 5, 56236, 5772, 5.464, 7.907, 5.3919, 3.293),
(371, 'Dairy', 'Description Take a photograph where the subject relates to milk or milk products.', '2005-08-17', '2005-08-23', '2005-08-24', '2005-08-30', 284, 6, 110249, 6687, 4.95185, 7.3256, 4.91645, 1.8805),
(372, 'D&L', 'Description Most of us know who "D&L" are on DPC, but what else could those initials stand for? Be creative, and title your shot with your D&L definition!', '2005-08-22', '2005-08-28', '2005-08-29', '2005-09-04', 200, 1, 50777, 3669, 5.561, 8.104, 5.5246, 3.391),
(373, 'Shoes', 'Description Shoes come in all varieties of textures, colors, sizes, and shapes. Don''t be a heel. Bare your sole and take an interesting photo of shoes.', '2005-08-24', '2005-08-30', '2005-08-31', '2005-09-06', 465, 10, 131897, 6902, 4.99751, 7.4601, 4.9418, 2.3891),
(374, 'High Contrast', 'Description Use high contrast to create impact in your photograph.', '2005-08-29', '2005-09-04', '2005-09-05', '2005-09-11', 343, 2, 83227, 4251, 5.437, 7.177, 5.4297, 3.131),
(375, 'Branch', 'Description A tree branch, a bank branch, a metaphorical branch. This word has many different meanings. Take a photograph relating to one of them.', '2005-08-31', '2005-09-06', '2005-09-07', '2005-09-13', 432, 12, 122766, 6792, 5.06811, 6.9806, 5.0632, 3.266),
(376, 'Color Portrait', 'Description Your submission must be in color (no B&W, duotones, sepia, etc.)', '2005-09-05', '2005-09-11', '2005-09-12', '2005-09-18', 284, 3, 84751, 6535, 5.36, 7.646, 5.2896, 3.065),
(377, 'Perspective II', 'Description Use perspective to create a dramatic effect with your photograph.', '2005-09-07', '2005-09-13', '2005-09-14', '2005-09-20', 544, 12, 143330, 5637, 5.25002, 7.6444, 5.2206, 2.7888),
(378, 'Destinations', 'Description You may be "here, now", but where will you end up? A destination may be a goal, or it may be something we fight against but gravitate towards. Give us a sense of where you dream of going, or where you''re fated to go.', '2005-09-12', '2005-09-18', '2005-09-19', '2005-09-25', 191, 5, 36515, 1955, 5.513, 7.314, 5.4381, 3.914),
(379, 'Bubbles', 'Description Bubbles, bubbles, bubbles! Let''s see your best shot of any sort of bubbles this week.', '2005-09-14', '2005-09-20', '2005-09-21', '2005-09-27', 240, 6, 71280, 2741, 5.07487, 7.2761, 5.0261, 2.6608),
(380, 'Rule of Thirds', 'Description The rule of thirds suggests that if you picture imaginary lines dividing your photograph in thirds (horizontally and vertically), your points of interest should be placed on the intersections of those lines. Your challenge is to take an interesting photograph using this technique.', '2005-09-14', '2005-09-20', '2005-09-21', '2005-09-27', 354, 6, 80777, 3543, 5.344, 7.345, 5.3265, 2.912),
(381, 'Conspiracy', 'Description Right wing, left wing, any-which-way-wing; let''s do the conspiracy thing with images instead of words, and give the poor forums a break! Show us your favorite conspiracy, if you dare.', '2005-09-16', '2005-09-17', '2005-09-18', '2005-09-24', 114, 2, 28408, 1663, 5.318, 7.086, 5.3, 4.301),
(382, 'Greeting Cards', 'Description Take a picture for one of those "blank inside" greeting cards. Your title should refer to the section the card would appear in the store, i.e. Birthday, Anniversary, Friendship, Sympathy, etc.', '2005-09-19', '2005-09-25', '2005-09-26', '2005-10-02', 211, 5, 45221, 2348, 5.396, 7.502, 5.3272, 3.45),
(383, 'From the Ground Up II', 'Description Take your best image from the perspective of the ground up.', '2005-09-21', '2005-09-27', '2005-09-28', '2005-10-04', 326, 5, 67132, 2472, 5.06931, 7.0317, 5.0076, 2.6065),
(384, 'Beverages', 'Description Your challenge this week is to creatively photograph any type of beverage.', '2005-09-21', '2005-09-27', '2005-09-28', '2005-10-04', 206, 6, 49379, 2071, 5.135, 6.955, 5.1686, 2.665),
(385, 'Your Corner of the World II', 'Description Photograph something that represents your corner of the world. This can be anything as small as something in your bedroom or as large as a city or state landmark.', '2005-09-26', '2005-10-02', '2005-10-03', '2005-10-09', 299, 4, 55319, 2441, 5.503, 7.462, 5.45575, 3.393),
(386, 'Coffee Shop', 'Description Take a photo that represents something you would find in a coffee shop. Let your imagination run wild.', '2005-09-28', '2005-10-04', '2005-10-05', '2005-10-11', 154, 1, 47967, 2528, 5.087, 7.038, 5.1904, 2.583),
(387, 'Complementary Colors II', 'Description While colors are fresh on your mind, try to use two complementary colors to compose your photograph.', '2005-09-28', '2005-10-04', '2005-10-05', '2005-10-11', 318, 5, 74281, 3401, 5.0795, 7.2258, 5.08955, 3.1079),
(388, 'Celebration', 'Description In a world of famine, poverty, war, and natural disasters it can sometimes be hard to stay upbeat. This week, let''s all find cause to celebrate. Devote your photographic energies to making us feel good about ourselves and our lives.', '2005-10-03', '2005-10-09', '2005-10-10', '2005-10-16', 137, 0, 28185, 2444, 5.342, 7.388, 5.26435, 3.699),
(389, 'Personification', 'Description Personification occurs when inanimate objects are endowed with human qualities or represented as possessing human form or personality. Take a photo of something non-human-looking but yet still shows human characteristics or evokes a human feeling.', '2005-10-05', '2005-10-11', '2005-10-12', '2005-10-18', 204, 4, 56320, 2845, 4.9258, 6.6862, 4.837, 2.9244),
(390, 'Pride', 'Description Photograph your interpretation of "Pride".', '2005-10-05', '2005-10-11', '2005-10-12', '2005-10-18', 158, 5, 39148, 1598, 5.137, 6.517, 5.1241, 2.478),
(391, 'Wide Angle', 'Description Technique Challenge: use the wide end of the lens built-in to your camera or the widest lens in your bag while taking your picture this week. Hint: you should avoid cropping, as this artificially "zooms in" on your picture.', '2005-10-10', '2005-10-16', '2005-10-17', '2005-10-23', 253, 1, 54823, 2602, 5.584, 7.453, 5.5674, 3.474),
(392, 'Reflections Without Mirrors II', 'Description Creatively photograph a reflecting surface that is not a mirror while keeping your camera out of the shot.', '2005-10-12', '2005-10-18', '2005-10-19', '2005-10-25', 371, 8, 102566, 4271, 5.17999, 7.1044, 5.167, 3.3463),
(393, 'What?', 'Description What!?', '2005-10-12', '2005-10-18', '2005-10-19', '2005-10-25', 274, 8, 58825, 2016, 5.129, 7.163, 5.08895, 3.593),
(394, 'Image Grain', 'Description Create an image where image grain or "noise" is an integral part of the message of your photo.', '2005-10-17', '2005-10-23', '2005-10-24', '2005-10-30', 274, 2, 51032, 2121, 5.285, 7.515, 5.2552, 3.856),
(395, 'Light On White II', 'Description Take a photo in which the background is white and the subject is predominately a "light" color. Be mindful of over-exposing your highlights!', '2005-10-19', '2005-10-25', '2005-10-26', '2005-11-01', 277, 8, 76934, 3073, 4.98583, 6.6213, 5.0302, 2.4754),
(396, 'Delicate', 'Description "Delicate" can mean so many things; easily damaged, easily wounded, ephemeral, finely made, difficult to handle, the list is long. What do YOU see when you picture the concept? Show us your delicate side.', '2005-10-19', '2005-10-25', '2005-10-26', '2005-11-01', 279, 11, 64289, 2585, 5.142, 7.457, 5.1342, 3.0),
(397, 'Transparency II', 'Description Use transparency to create the impact of your photo this week.', '2005-10-24', '2005-10-30', '2005-10-31', '2005-11-06', 155, 0, 31417, 2004, 5.433, 7.05, 5.3576, 3.746),
(398, 'Busy', 'Description From telephone signals to distracting design elements, there are lots of ways for something to be "busy". Do your best to represent some form of busy in the challenge photograph you take this week.', '2005-10-26', '2005-11-01', '2005-11-02', '2005-11-08', 190, 5, 47256, 1855, 5.14, 7.215, 5.1008, 2.739),
(399, 'Shutter Speed', 'Description Create an image where your choice of shutter speed leads to the main impact. Choose fast shutter speeds to freeze motion or slow ones to capture motion blur.', '2005-10-26', '2005-11-01', '2005-11-02', '2005-11-08', 296, 3, 76655, 2667, 5.15302, 7.3978, 5.1395, 2.9515),
(400, 'The Great Pumpkin Carving Challenge', 'Description Your challenge is to carve and photograph a pumpkin or pumpkins. Team pumpkins are allowed (work with friends or family if you like) but PLEASE have at least a hand in the carving yourself. The honor system is in effect on this one; we''re not going to be Big Brother, but we want your own, unique, personal pumpkin. This challenge is as much about the pumpkin as it is about the photography. Please be careful when using sharp implements.', '2005-10-28', '2005-10-31', '2005-11-01', '2005-11-07', 88, 1, 19598, 1292, 5.833, 7.543, 5.736, 4.444),
(401, 'Free Study IX', 'Description The long-awaited and much-anticipated return of the Free Study. Good luck!', '2005-11-01', '2005-11-30', '2005-12-01', '2005-12-07', 519, 6, 144059, 6481, 5.534, 7.831, 5.5237, 3.353),
(402, 'Dead End', 'Description Creatively photograph a dead end. It can be a dead end street, hall, maze, or a metaphoric dead end -- you decide.', '2005-10-31', '2005-11-06', '2005-11-07', '2005-11-13', 173, 2, 34701, 1626, 5.459, 7.219, 5.37395, 3.84),
(403, 'Landscape II', 'Description This is a classic area of photography that needs little explanation. Do your best to make your photograph as refreshing as you can. Good luck!', '2005-11-02', '2005-11-08', '2005-11-09', '2005-11-15', 403, 7, 132884, 5630, 5.341, 7.27, 5.3373, 2.079),
(404, 'Garbage II', 'Description Garbage! Garbage is everywhere. Compose your best photograph of garbage, trash, or waste this week.', '2005-11-02', '2005-11-08', '2005-11-09', '2005-11-15', 212, 5, 53459, 2292, 5.03741, 6.5115, 5.0059, 2.9887);
INSERT INTO challenges ("id", "name", "description", "submission_start", "submission_end", "voting_start", "voting_end", "num_submissions", "num_disqualifications", "num_votes", "num_comments", "average_score", "highest_score", "median_score", "lowest_score") VALUES
(405, 'Triptych', 'Description A triptych is a work of art which is divided into three sections and then hinged or connected. Create an entry consisting of three panels that tells a story or illustrates a concept or object. Your panels can be made up of one photo or up to three separate photos.', '2005-11-07', '2005-11-13', '2005-11-14', '2005-11-20', 234, 5, 61099, 3312, 5.649, 7.365, 5.6455, 3.912),
(406, 'Single Light Source', 'Description Use a single, artificial light source to dramatically light the subject of your choice.', '2005-11-09', '2005-11-15', '2005-11-16', '2005-11-22', 291, 10, 80782, 3225, 5.08164, 6.8135, 5.06965, 3.3456),
(407, 'Camouflage', 'Description Camouflage is used to conceal something through the use of disguise, coloring or misrepresentation.', '2005-11-09', '2005-11-15', '2005-11-16', '2005-11-22', 169, 2, 49606, 2468, 5.261, 7.355, 5.1783, 3.2),
(408, 'Cheater!', 'Description Deception is the name of the game. Show someone or something that clearly isn''t playing by the rules. (Yes, the challenge rules still apply).', '2005-11-14', '2005-11-20', '2005-11-21', '2005-11-27', 105, 4, 22348, 1024, 5.385, 7.298, 5.30295, 3.883),
(409, 'Even', 'Description Numbers, length, matchups... find a creative way to photograph the concept of "even"', '2005-11-16', '2005-11-22', '2005-11-23', '2005-11-29', 152, 3, 45883, 1971, 5.24266, 7.4416, 5.20295, 3.6977),
(410, 'Odd', 'Description Numbers, strange... find a creative way to photograph the concept of "odd"', '2005-11-16', '2005-11-22', '2005-11-23', '2005-11-29', 223, 2, 50355, 1913, 5.055, 6.987, 5.0298, 2.441),
(411, 'Adulthood Without Adults', 'Description To complement the Childhood Without Children challenge, take a photo that represents adulthood, without having any adults in the picture. Be creative!', '2005-11-21', '2005-11-27', '2005-11-28', '2005-12-04', 105, 0, 23555, 1056, 5.29, 6.555, 5.28045, 4.203),
(412, 'Collections', 'Description Stamps, coins, dolls, cars, shoes... people will collect just about anything. Let''s see what makes your particular collection special.', '2005-11-23', '2005-11-29', '2005-11-30', '2005-12-06', 210, 8, 54390, 2833, 5.03666, 7.0584, 5.0383, 2.7054),
(413, 'Industrial', 'Description Photograph something that has an "industrial" feeling.', '2005-11-23', '2005-11-29', '2005-11-30', '2005-12-06', 223, 1, 58554, 2161, 5.348, 7.424, 5.3867, 2.679),
(414, 'Knife Fork Spoon', 'Description Take your best photo of any (or all) of these three. Don''t forget that there are multiple meanings to these words!', '2005-11-28', '2005-12-04', '2005-12-05', '2005-12-11', 163, 2, 31509, 1721, 5.442, 7.054, 5.3867, 3.604),
(415, 'Too Early', 'Description Compose a photograph and shoot it as if you were too early.', '2005-11-30', '2005-12-06', '2005-12-07', '2005-12-13', 109, 5, 31836, 1749, 5.13563, 6.7726, 5.1411, 3.0687),
(416, 'Too Late', 'Description Compose a photograph and shoot it as if you were too late.', '2005-11-30', '2005-12-06', '2005-12-07', '2005-12-13', 168, 4, 35649, 1594, 5.044, 7.076, 5.0821, 3.069),
(417, 'Candlelight', 'Description It can be romantic, nostalgic, fun or just plain spooky. Use candlelight to create the impact of your photo.', '2005-12-05', '2005-12-11', '2005-12-12', '2005-12-18', 160, 2, 32352, 1551, 5.316, 7.156, 5.2981, 3.871),
(418, 'Holiday Catalog', 'Description From scented candles for Aunt Wilma to festive socks for Uncle Fred. Capture the spirit of the holidays like only a catalog can. Be creative and have fun!', '2005-12-10', '2005-12-11', '2005-12-12', '2005-12-18', 120, 1, 22003, 1126, 5.426, 7.01, 5.40485, 3.667),
(419, '4:00-5:00 a.m.', 'Description Set your alarm, and take a picture between 4:00 and 5:00 AM. This challenge may also be known as the "I can''t believe I got up this early to take a photograph for a ^$&@*# challenge" challenge.', '2005-12-07', '2005-12-13', '2005-12-14', '2005-12-20', 115, 2, 41136, 2059, 5.371, 8.311, 5.3778, 3.1),
(420, 'Say Cheese!', 'Description The old photographer''s cliché is now a challenge topic. Use cheese as the subject of your photo to make your audience smile.', '2005-12-07', '2005-12-13', '2005-12-14', '2005-12-20', 107, 2, 28798, 1590, 4.903, 6.957, 4.9644, 2.563),
(421, 'Visual Puns', 'Description "Relief - what trees do in the spring." A pun is a play on words which have a similar sound but different meanings. Now it''s your turn to take a photograph that visually represents a different application of a word or words.', '2005-12-12', '2005-12-18', '2005-12-19', '2005-12-25', 144, 4, 31759, 1374, 5.575, 7.587, 5.5289, 4.096),
(422, 'Phobia', 'Description Photograph something in such a way that it conveys a personal phobia or fear to the viewer. Try to make the viewer feel the emotion of the fear. No bugs (including spiders), as that is just too easy! Your title or description should include your phobia. A list of phobias can be found here: phobialist.com.', '2005-12-14', '2005-12-20', '2005-12-21', '2005-12-27', 144, 7, 39603, 1942, 5.313, 7.864, 5.25045, 3.227),
