(2392, 'Tribute to Dorothea Lange', 'Description Dorothea Lange was one of the most respected and influential photographers of the 20th century. Her unsentimental yet compassionate eye gave us enduring images of America''s great depression and the dust bowl years.', '2016-11-28', '2016-12-11', '2016-12-12', '2016-12-18', 26, 1, 1492, 83, 6.06501, 7.3036, 5.9298, 4.9649),
(2393, 'Pareidolia II', 'Description Pareidolia is a psychological phenomenon involving a vague and random stimulus (often an image or sound) being perceived as significant. Common examples include seeing images of animals or faces in clouds, the man in the moon, and hearing hidden messages on records played in reverse. Capture a real world example of this phenomenon. Your subject should not be created specifically for this challenge - buildings, bridges and other man-made objects are OK, as long as it is not an object specifically fashioned for the challenge to look significant.', '2016-11-30', '2016-12-13', '2016-12-14', '2016-12-20', 35, 1, 1942, 100, 5.61071, 6.6379, 5.6271, 4.3929),
(2394, 'Free Study 2016-12', 'Description Free Study for December, 2016.', '2016-12-01', '2016-12-31', '2017-01-01', '2017-01-07', 89, 1, 6465, 476, 5.70719, 7.6133, 5.6757, 4.4247),
(2395, 'Vanishing Point IV', 'Description Vanishing points: go capture one before it disappears.', '2016-12-02', '2016-12-15', '2016-12-16', '2016-12-22', 46, 0, 2034, 67, 5.65093, 7.1818, 5.4651, 4.2273),
(2396, 'Wallflower', 'Description N/A', '2016-12-05', '2016-12-18', '2016-12-19', '2016-12-25', 29, 0, 1220, 32, 5.19754, 6.2558, 5.2262, 4.025),
(2397, 'Ugly to Lovely', 'Description Take what most might consider "ugly" and make it "lovely" by the way you photograph it.', '2016-12-07', '2016-12-20', '2016-12-21', '2016-12-27', 37, 0, 2006, 20, 5.15553, 6.2115, 5.1994, 3.9464),
(2398, 'One Photo', 'Description Yesterday, a probe was sent to the planet''s surface. It sent back only one image before communications were lost. Ladies and gentlemen, here is that photograph...', '2016-12-09', '2016-12-22', '2016-12-23', '2016-12-29', 35, 1, 1893, 74, 5.64184, 7.4815, 5.61465, 4.3148),
(2399, 'Trees VII', 'Description N/A', '2016-12-12', '2016-12-25', '2016-12-26', '2017-01-01', 50, 0, 3072, 172, 5.58008, 7.2381, 5.5323, 4.4355),
(2400, 'All is Calm, All is Bright', 'Description ''Tis the season...', '2016-12-14', '2016-12-27', '2016-12-28', '2017-01-03', 44, 0, 2718, 305, 5.64422, 7.1429, 5.5574, 3.7097),
(2401, 'Extended Free Study 2016-12', 'Description Extended Free Study for December, 2016.', '2016-12-15', '2017-01-14', '2017-01-15', '2017-01-21', 55, 0, 2893, 95, 5.68787, 7.3846, 5.63805, 4.1509),
(2402, 'Postage Stamp II', 'Description Mail is so old, it''s time to pay homage. Pick a country, take a photo, engage your design aesthetic. Show us an original design for a postage stamp.', '2016-12-16', '2016-12-29', '2016-12-30', '2017-01-05', 29, 1, 1443, 155, 5.92169, 7.9615, 6.0392, 4.0962),
(2403, 'Make it Square', 'Description Your image must be square. If it isn''t, it''s a DQ.', '2016-12-19', '2017-01-01', '2017-01-02', '2017-01-08', 57, 1, 2831, 131, 5.6224, 6.9388, 5.5921, 4.24),
(2404, 'Snapshot II', 'Description Let''s do snapshots like it''s still 1965 and we just dropped a roll of film off to the drugstore to be processed :-)', '2016-12-21', '2017-01-03', '2017-01-04', '2017-01-10', 64, 2, 3536, 155, 5.63094, 6.4815, 5.57645, 4.7679),
(2405, 'Holiday Cheer', 'Description The decorations, the lights, the feast, the libations... It''s that time of year!', '2016-12-23', '2017-01-05', '2017-01-06', '2017-01-12', 52, 0, 2086, 122, 5.56088, 7.3, 5.55, 3.8462),
(2406, 'Get Mechanical', 'Description N/A', '2016-12-26', '2017-01-08', '2017-01-09', '2017-01-15', 49, 0, 2768, 85, 5.53974, 6.5345, 5.6607, 3.9474),
(2407, 'New Year''s Resolution IX', 'Description We''re giving you plenty of time to come up with a resolution and illustrate it for us. Have fun! Be good! Happy New Year, all!', '2016-12-28', '2017-01-10', '2017-01-11', '2017-01-17', 55, 0, 3556, 191, 5.63723, 7.1818, 5.6797, 4.2),
(2408, 'The Eyes Have It! II', 'Description It''s said the eye is the window to the soul. Certainly, eyes are compelling and mysterious, and they are among the most challenging features to photograph well. Give us a look at your best eyes, animal or human.', '2016-12-30', '2017-01-12', '2017-01-13', '2017-01-19', 50, 0, 3085, 115, 5.45867, 7.0484, 5.5645, 3.7049),
(2409, 'Free Study 2017-01', 'Description Free Study for January, 2017.', '2017-01-01', '2017-01-31', '2017-02-01', '2017-02-07', 120, 1, 8213, 403, 5.56934, 6.8475, 5.6286, 3.942),
(2410, 'First Impressions  Land-or-Cityscape, 2017', 'Description Have a look around you, and show us what the New Year looks like in your corner of the world.', '2017-01-02', '2017-01-15', '2017-01-16', '2017-01-22', 62, 0, 3471, 143, 5.7724, 7.4, 5.7895, 4.2143),
(2411, 'Art of 2016', 'Description Take a look backward as the New Year dawns and mine your archives for artistic gems.', '2017-01-04', '2017-01-17', '2017-01-18', '2017-01-24', 150, 2, 15169, 938, 5.51632, 6.6893, 5.5429, 3.9293),
(2412, 'If I Were an Animal', 'Description Show us what you''d look like... if ... YOU were... an animal. You''ve gotta start with a photo of you.', '2017-01-06', '2017-01-19', '2017-01-20', '2017-01-26', 19, 0, 1148, 98, 5.98084, 7.2833, 6.00885, 4.9016),
(2413, 'Abstract Expressionism', 'Description In the style of Aaron Siskind, one of the first photographers to combine what was known as "straight" photography (recording the real world as the lens "sees" it) with abstraction.', '2017-01-09', '2017-01-22', '2017-01-23', '2017-01-29', 74, 0, 4156, 132, 5.5089, 6.614, 5.5926, 4.1579),
(2414, 'Juxtaposed II', 'Description N/A', '2017-01-11', '2017-01-24', '2017-01-25', '2017-01-31', 56, 0, 3391, 144, 5.48599, 6.8852, 5.4426, 4.4576),
(2415, 'Friday the 13th II', 'Description N/A', '2017-01-13', '2017-01-26', '2017-01-27', '2017-02-02', 26, 0, 1466, 85, 5.35471, 7.1786, 5.2105, 4.0),
(2416, 'Extended Free Study 2017-01', 'Description Extended Free Study for January, 2017.', '2017-01-15', '2017-02-14', '2017-02-15', '2017-02-21', 67, 0, 3988, 190, 5.54814, 6.9839, 5.5041, 4.1803),
(2417, 'Title Tale', 'Description A picture may be worth a thousand words, but some images work best when they don''t stand alone. Submit a photo that depends on the title for explanation or impact.', '2017-01-16', '2017-01-29', '2017-01-30', '2017-02-05', 53, 1, 3138, 64, 5.55226, 6.9661, 5.64705, 4.5);
INSERT INTO challenges ("id", "name", "description", "submission_start", "submission_end", "voting_start", "voting_end", "num_submissions", "num_disqualifications", "num_votes", "num_comments", "average_score", "highest_score", "median_score", "lowest_score") VALUES
(2418, 'Supermarket Still Life', 'Description Source your Still Life from the supermarket or grocery store.', '2017-01-18', '2017-01-31', '2017-02-01', '2017-02-07', 36, 3, 2056, 152, 5.1216, 6.4407, 4.9474, 4.3115),
(2419, 'Burst of Color V', 'Description Use color expressively to help your subject stand out from the rest of your image.', '2017-01-20', '2017-02-02', '2017-02-03', '2017-02-09', 56, 1, 3054, 117, 5.43811, 6.5789, 5.4545, 3.3273),
(2420, 'Best of 2016', 'Description Show us the best shot you took last year! That is, the best shot that you did not already submit to a challenge. Good luck!', '2017-01-19', '2017-01-31', '2017-02-01', '2017-02-07', 131, 1, 8631, 199, 5.60457, 6.8857, 5.5915, 3.8676),
(2421, 'Whatever the Weather', 'Description Just show us the whatever the weather is wherever you are today.', '2017-01-23', '2017-02-05', '2017-02-06', '2017-02-12', 81, 0, 5306, 170, 5.47776, 6.6984, 5.4889, 4.4531),
(2422, 'Katie Melua Song Lyrics', 'Description Katie Melua is a prolific songwriter with loads of visually interesting ''images'' in her lyrics. Let''s get inspired by her.', '2017-01-25', '2017-02-07', '2017-02-08', '2017-02-14', 40, 3, 2180, 111, 5.5789, 6.661, 5.5763, 4.3966),
(2423, 'Lifestyle Portrait', 'Description Create a photo that communicates someone''s lifestyle.', '2017-01-27', '2017-02-09', '2017-02-10', '2017-02-16', 40, 0, 2256, 92, 5.58112, 6.6316, 5.6604, 4.0545),
(2424, 'Puzzle Macro VI', 'Description Take a macro photo of something, and try to stump the viewer as to what it actually is. Your title should NOT identify or even hint at what the object is, but you should include a description of your object in the photographer details field.', '2017-01-30', '2017-02-12', '2017-02-13', '2017-02-19', 72, 1, 5166, 1160, 5.48703, 7.1053, 5.48315, 4.2083),
(2425, 'Free Study 2017-02', 'Description Free Study for February, 2017.', '2017-02-01', '2017-02-28', '2017-03-01', '2017-03-07', 123, 1, 8585, 197, 5.52149, 6.8028, 5.5556, 4.1268),
(2426, 'Camera Movement II', 'Description Move your camera during your shot to create an interesting effect. Shake it, pan it, whirl it, bounce it, toss it, drop it, flop it, rip it, grip it like death and give in to your tremors; if your camera was moving, you''ve met the challenge :-)', '2017-02-01', '2017-02-14', '2017-02-15', '2017-02-21', 69, 0, 4189, 135, 5.61876, 6.7619, 5.6084, 3.9167),
(2427, 'Communication II', 'Description Communication: the passing of ideas or information from one person or group to another.', '2017-02-03', '2017-02-16', '2017-02-17', '2017-02-23', 36, 1, 1786, 88, 5.58063, 6.6122, 5.5806, 4.3673),
(2428, 'Ruckus', 'Description A few levels short of mayhem. Photograph some sort of conflict or disturbance in public or private, human or animal.', '2017-02-06', '2017-02-19', '2017-02-20', '2017-02-26', 30, 0, 1835, 108, 5.40436, 7.129, 5.3387, 3.871),
(2429, 'Hearty Fun', 'Description Celebrate Valentine''s Day by seeking out heart shapes in the natural world. Check out rocks, tree branches, leaves, bark, cloud formations, wherever you might find an engaging heart. Please, no set-up shots for this challenge...', '2017-02-08', '2017-02-21', '2017-02-22', '2017-02-28', 44, 0, 2430, 75, 5.36379, 6.7647, 5.4737, 3.4727),
(2431, 'Minimalist Landscape III', 'Description Find a simple, uncluttered, natural vista and give it your best shot.', '2017-02-10', '2017-02-23', '2017-02-24', '2017-03-02', 61, 0, 3701, 162, 5.65982, 6.8906, 5.6585, 4.1053),
(2432, 'Pink and/or Red', 'Description Either color, or both, should be prominent in your image. The catch? This is MINIMAL editing, so get it right in-camera.', '2017-02-13', '2017-02-26', '2017-02-27', '2017-03-05', 63, 0, 4122, 119, 5.5393, 6.7538, 5.41955, 4.3443),
(2433, 'Extended Free Study 2017-02', 'Description Extended Free Study for February, 2017.', '2017-02-15', '2017-03-14', '2017-03-15', '2017-03-21', 61, 0, 2723, 97, 5.85237, 7.087, 5.84415, 4.7209),
(2434, 'Soft Focus, High Key', 'Description N/A', '2017-02-15', '2017-02-28', '2017-03-01', '2017-03-07', 65, 1, 4081, 104, 5.42441, 6.5846, 5.4754, 3.1094),
(2435, 'Art in the Incidental', 'Description It shows up where you least expect it; hunt some down and bring it home :-)', '2017-02-17', '2017-03-02', '2017-03-03', '2017-03-09', 62, 0, 3063, 228, 5.64349, 6.4314, 5.6042, 4.9583),
(2436, 'As-Found Filter', 'Description Use a found object of some sort as a filter in front of your lens and see what happens!', '2017-02-20', '2017-03-05', '2017-03-06', '2017-03-12', 41, 0, 1980, 76, 5.61515, 6.5319, 5.61045, 4.6667),
(2437, 'Battle of the Sexes II', 'Description Men are from Mars, women are from Venus: small wonder that the "battle of the sexes" is always with us. Show us your take on this ageless theme. It''s been 10 years since we ran this the first time; has anything changed?', '2017-02-22', '2017-03-07', '2017-03-08', '2017-03-14', 22, 0, 1269, 40, 5.40662, 6.4035, 5.2807, 3.9828),
(2438, 'Chimera', 'Description In mythology, the chimera was a fire-breathing monster, commonly represented with a lion''s head, a goat''s body, and a serpent''s tail. In biology, the more generalized meaning is an organism, tissue, cell or molecule formed by fusing genetically different parts together. In your challenge entry, fuse together 2 or more different things to achieve an interesting hybrid. For example, it could be 2 animals or it could be 3 tools or it could be a person and a car. The fusion can be seamless, or it can be slapped together. Use the title to give your new creation a name.', '2017-02-24', '2017-03-09', '2017-03-10', '2017-03-16', 17, 0, 902, 35, 5.82483, 7.0926, 5.7327, 4.6731),
(2439, 'Music IV', 'Description Create an image that sings of "music" in the viewer''s eye.', '2017-02-27', '2017-03-12', '2017-03-13', '2017-03-19', 50, 0, 2347, 54, 5.50149, 6.6957, 5.4792, 4.3111),
(2440, 'Free Study 2017-03', 'Description Free Study for March, 2017.', '2017-03-01', '2017-03-31', '2017-04-01', '2017-04-07', 106, 3, 4837, 177, 5.45297, 6.9388, 5.5, 3.9),
(2441, 'Black and White Landscape III', 'Description Create a black and white photo of a landscape (either urban or rural).', '2017-03-01', '2017-03-14', '2017-03-15', '2017-03-21', 82, 0, 4789, 131, 5.51263, 6.8361, 5.4182, 4.1404),
(2442, 'Philias & Phobias', 'Description Where "phobia" is an irrational or obsessive fear of something in specific, its antonym, "philia", denotes a liking or friendship. Show us one or the other, or both at once.', '2017-03-03', '2017-03-16', '2017-03-17', '2017-03-23', 45, 0, 1875, 55, 5.65067, 7.3256, 5.6032, 4.425),
(2443, 'Implied Lines II', 'Description The human eye is very good at seeing lines, whether they really exist or not. Take a photograph that uses implied lines (for example, the "line" made by a row of trees) as a compositional element.', '2017-03-06', '2017-03-19', '2017-03-20', '2017-03-26', 47, 1, 1857, 57, 5.5972, 6.7561, 5.6098, 4.3846),
(2444, 'Over-Saturated & Over-Sharpened', 'Description Give us an interesting image that is enhanced by its over-saturation and/or over-sharpening. It may SOUND hideous to you, but there''s a huge amount of leeway for creativity when you go totally out-of-bounds :-)', '2017-03-08', '2017-03-21', '2017-03-22', '2017-03-28', 87, 1, 4480, 99, 5.48348, 7.0, 5.48075, 4.0196),
(2445, 'St. Green Saves The Earth!', 'Description In honor of Earth Day and Saint Paddy''s Day, let''s get minimal and find a way to celebrate either or both of the holidays by going green.', '2017-03-10', '2017-03-23', '2017-03-24', '2017-03-30', 36, 0, 1576, 62, 5.53299, 6.913, 5.4419, 4.3721),
(2446, 'Peace II', 'Description N/A', '2017-03-13', '2017-03-26', '2017-03-27', '2017-04-02', 40, 0, 1661, 47, 5.472, 6.3659, 5.4878, 4.4878),
(2447, 'Defining Feature III', 'Description We often remember people for the little things about them or their personality, what makes them who they are. Find someone, figure out what defines them, and illustrate it for us. Title your entry with the feature you are illustrating.', '2017-03-15', '2017-03-28', '2017-03-29', '2017-04-04', 34, 0, 1639, 57, 5.57718, 6.7917, 5.6939, 3.2917),
(2448, 'Extended Free Study 2017-03', 'Description Extended Free Study for March, 2017.', '2017-03-15', '2017-04-14', '2017-04-15', '2017-04-21', 49, 0, 2510, 107, 5.89442, 7.3585, 5.9119, 4.4),
(2449, 'Myths, Legends, and Fables', 'Description N/A', '2017-03-17', '2017-03-30', '2017-03-31', '2017-04-06', 38, 0, 1912, 83, 5.85042, 7.0769, 5.8077, 4.6),
(2450, 'Pattern VI', 'Description Patterns are found everywhere. Find a pattern that captures your attention and hopefully ours as well.', '2017-03-20', '2017-04-02', '2017-04-03', '2017-04-09', 69, 1, 2957, 109, 5.54447, 6.8636, 5.5116, 4.381),
(2451, 'What is this Pencil II', 'Description Take a photo that has a pencil as its subject. However, the pencil must be used or communicated as something other than a pencil in the photo.', '2017-03-22', '2017-04-04', '2017-04-05', '2017-04-11', 33, 0, 1827, 154, 5.71593, 7.1455, 5.6727, 4.4464),
(2452, 'Anatopism', 'Description An anatopism (from the Greek ανα, "against," and τόπος, "place") is something that is out of its proper place. Thus, for example, a Polynesian outrigger canoe would be an anatopism in a lake in Bavaria. The concept of anatopism is less widely familiar than that of anachronism, perhaps because much that is anatopistic is also anachronistic. Yet the distinction is a valid one; not all that is anatopistic is necessarily also anachronistic.', '2017-03-24', '2017-04-06', '2017-04-07', '2017-04-13', 29, 0, 1322, 81, 5.6528, 6.5652, 5.56165, 4.1111),
(2453, 'What Makes Me Happy', 'Description Show us!', '2017-03-27', '2017-04-09', '2017-04-10', '2017-04-16', 60, 1, 2904, 195, 5.6436, 6.72, 5.66105, 3.7959),
(2454, 'Emptiness', 'Description The empty glass. The forsaken heart. The barren landscape. The dark night of the soul. Show us emptiness.', '2017-03-29', '2017-04-11', '2017-04-12', '2017-04-18', 68, 0, 5369, 102, 5.50736, 6.5, 5.4872, 4.3038),
(2455, 'Show Us Some Teeth', 'Description N/A', '2017-03-31', '2017-04-13', '2017-04-14', '2017-04-20', 25, 0, 1351, 89, 5.81865, 6.6981, 5.7407, 4.2037),
(2456, 'Free Study 2017-04', 'Description Free Study for April, 2017.', '2017-04-01', '2017-04-30', '2017-05-01', '2017-05-07', 128, 0, 8459, 285, 5.66013, 6.9032, 5.6176, 4.6087),
(2457, 'slooF lirpA', 'Description N/A', '2017-04-01', '2017-04-02', '2017-04-03', '2017-04-09', 31, 0, 1498, 36, 5.56676, 7.44, 5.42665, 4.9375),
(2458, 'Silhouettes VIII', 'Description A Silhouette results when objects are backlit, causing them to appear solid and without much, if any detail. This week, shoot into the light!', '2017-04-03', '2017-04-16', '2017-04-17', '2017-04-23', 59, 0, 3380, 145, 5.68521, 7.5965, 5.61205, 4.1754),
(2459, 'Colorful', 'Description N/A', '2017-04-05', '2017-04-18', '2017-04-19', '2017-04-25', 64, 2, 4010, 74, 5.57032, 6.9365, 5.6333, 3.7538),
(2460, 'Wabi Sabi', 'Description Looking at the everyday, at the commonplace, and finding magic in them  a reminder that nothing in life, or design, is perfect. It is about appreciating the aesthetic concept of wabi-sabi, finding it or seeing it in things that already exist in the visual world around us.', '2017-04-07', '2017-04-20', '2017-04-21', '2017-04-27', 61, 0, 3144, 109, 5.63677, 6.6852, 5.6107, 4.64),
(2461, 'Squats & Lifts', 'Description This challenge is all about POV: take on one of your preferred subjects, but approach it from a lower or higher vantage point than you normally would. No drone or airplane shots, please.', '2017-04-10', '2017-04-23', '2017-04-24', '2017-04-30', 60, 0, 2825, 111, 5.7285, 7.0851, 5.6596, 4.6383),
(2462, 'Good Grooming', 'Description Anything & everything related to looking sharp.', '2017-04-12', '2017-04-25', '2017-04-26', '2017-05-02', 28, 1, 1698, 61, 5.44405, 6.1935, 5.4667, 3.8448),
(2463, 'Still Life VI', 'Description It''s time to revisit this classic theme; study up on the genre and try your hand at one yourself.', '2017-04-14', '2017-04-27', '2017-04-28', '2017-05-04', 43, 0, 2194, 112, 5.43665, 6.56, 5.48585, 4.0),
(2464, 'Extended Free Study 2017-04', 'Description Extended Free Study for April, 2017.', '2017-04-15', '2017-05-14', '2017-05-15', '2017-05-21', 63, 0, 3368, 102, 5.76366, 7.4717, 5.7407, 4.2909),
(2465, 'Graffiti II', 'Description "Graffiti" is defined as "writing or drawings scribbled, scratched, or sprayed illicitly on a wall or other surface in a public place." Find some and photograph it :-)', '2017-04-17', '2017-04-30', '2017-05-01', '2017-05-07', 32, 4, 1295, 58, 5.43475, 6.087, 5.4222, 4.6364),
(2466, 'Light & Architecture: the Joy of Structure', 'Description Wynn Bullock spoke of this: "Not form rock, not object rock, but the light that IS the rock." Architects work with light as much as with material and space, and in a very real sense without light there is no architecture. Show us the joy of light & form.', '2017-04-19', '2017-05-02', '2017-05-03', '2017-05-09', 46, 0, 2873, 36, 5.62757, 7.0645, 5.6349, 3.6984),
(2467, 'Sci-Fi Celebration II', 'Description Science Fiction - John Wyndham, Isaac Asimov, Brian Aldiss, Arthur C. Clarke, Edgar Rice Burroughs - show us your aliens, spacecraft, Midwitchers, Triffids, space costumes, UFOs, homes of the future, space stations, future foods, the universe is your oyster!', '2017-04-21', '2017-05-04', '2017-05-05', '2017-05-11', 26, 1, 1173, 81, 5.4561, 6.7174, 5.3913, 4.5208),
(2468, 'In The Style Of: Melethia', 'Description Check out Deb/Melethia''s portfolio, and revel in the simple pleasure of viewing the world through a friendly and discerning eye.', '2017-04-24', '2017-05-07', '2017-05-08', '2017-05-14', 58, 0, 3322, 392, 5.81126, 7.3621, 5.7544, 4.931),
(2469, 'Deep DOF III', 'Description Take control of your aperture this week and photograph a scene where everything is in focus.', '2017-04-26', '2017-05-09', '2017-05-10', '2017-05-16', 51, 0, 3511, 187, 5.75164, 7.029, 5.82735, 4.1594),
(2470, 'Cat People/Dog People', 'Description Some people love cats, others are loyal to their dogs. Show us some cat people or dog people and the animals they bond with.', '2017-04-28', '2017-05-11', '2017-05-12', '2017-05-18', 35, 0, 2180, 173, 5.88899, 7.619, 5.9206, 4.6557),
(2471, 'Free Study 2017-05', 'Description Free Study for May, 2017.', '2017-05-01', '2017-05-31', '2017-06-01', '2017-06-07', 114, 0, 5898, 189, 5.598, 6.8444, 5.6222, 3.6607),
(2472, 'Window View III', 'Description Find an interesting window view. The window glass or frame must be included in the photo to make it obvious it''s been taken from a window.', '2017-05-01', '2017-05-14', '2017-05-15', '2017-05-21', 48, 1, 2237, 88, 5.70988, 6.7708, 5.8061, 4.1489),
(2473, 'Spring or Fall', 'Description Spring is springing in the north, and fall is falling in the south. Wherever you are, show us what it''s like :-)', '2017-05-03', '2017-05-16', '2017-05-17', '2017-05-23', 57, 0, 3190, 70, 5.43166, 6.614, 5.5398, 2.9298),
(2474, 'Crummy Weather', 'Description Watching the news channels, it seems like much of the world is suffering some sort of yucky/uncomfortable/miserable/just-plain-crummy weather at the moment. Let''s take advantage of it! Show us YOUR crummy weather.', '2017-05-05', '2017-05-18', '2017-05-19', '2017-05-25', 41, 0, 2077, 115, 5.74579, 7.3269, 5.6273, 4.451),
(2475, 'Off Color', 'Description Blue lobsters, purple carrots, and albino cardinals? Find and shoot a natural subject that''s not its expected color.', '2017-05-08', '2017-05-21', '2017-05-22', '2017-05-28', 22, 1, 909, 61, 5.53795, 6.6512, 5.472, 4.0),
(2476, 'The Secret Life of Food', 'Description Take a creative photo that shows what your fruit, cereal or other food does when nobody is looking.', '2017-05-10', '2017-05-23', '2017-05-24', '2017-05-30', 21, 0, 1354, 96, 6.01108, 7.1875, 6.11685, 4.4462),
(2477, 'Wildlife VII', 'Description For the purpose of this challenge, "wildlife" should be considered non-domesticated mammals, birds, reptiles and amphibians living in a natural environment.', '2017-05-12', '2017-05-25', '2017-05-26', '2017-06-01', 54, 1, 3089, 322, 5.76497, 7.4746, 5.7119, 4.4237),
(2478, 'Night Sky III', 'Description Use the moon, stars or planets to create a photo that''s out of this world! The visual impact of your image should be heavily dependent on your depiction of the night sky.', '2017-05-15', '2017-05-28', '2017-05-29', '2017-06-04', 19, 0, 1285, 60, 5.95175, 7.8636, 5.7785, 4.7463),
(2479, 'Extended Free Study 2017-05', 'Description Extended Free Study for May, 2017.', '2017-05-15', '2017-06-14', '2017-06-15', '2017-06-21', 53, 0, 2575, 62, 5.6967, 6.7083, 5.7245, 4.3061),
(2480, 'Breaking the Rules', 'Description There are many implied "rules" for "good" photography: "use the rule of thirds", "don''t shoot into the sun" and "keep the subject sharp" are just three of them. But rules are made to be broken! Break a photography rule and make it work. Your title should tell us the rule you are breaking with your entry.', '2017-05-17', '2017-05-30', '2017-05-31', '2017-06-06', 66, 0, 3992, 184, 5.5486, 6.6667, 5.5, 4.3934),
(2481, 'The Crowd', 'Description A crowd is generally considered a large gathering of people  find a crowd and capture a photo that shows its true nature.', '2017-05-19', '2017-06-01', '2017-06-02', '2017-06-08', 35, 0, 1654, 70, 5.49516, 6.7083, 5.53125, 4.25),
(2482, 'Flowers IV', 'Description Your challenge is simple -- photograph one or more flowers.', '2017-05-22', '2017-06-04', '2017-06-05', '2017-06-11', 82, 1, 4269, 228, 5.48817, 6.3704, 5.4996, 4.4074),
(2483, 'In the Style of Vincent Van Gogh', 'Description Study the art of this Impressionist master and distill his way of seeing in a photograph.', '2017-05-24', '2017-06-06', '2017-06-07', '2017-06-13', 60, 0, 2859, 56, 5.42462, 7.2653, 5.3261, 4.4565),
(2484, 'Tracks', 'Description Animal tracks, tire tracks, footprints, or even breadcrumbs... leave your mark on DPC with a creative take on this unique subject.', '2017-05-26', '2017-06-08', '2017-06-09', '2017-06-15', 37, 0, 1595, 42, 5.53166, 6.8571, 5.48285, 4.186),
(2485, 'Remembering', 'Description We''ve all lost someone close to us, and we all have our ways of remembering. Often physical objects, certain places, specific songs, etc act as emotional "triggers" that bring our memories to the surface. Try to show us this in a photograph. Your title should be the name of the person you are honoring/remembering.', '2017-05-29', '2017-06-11', '2017-06-12', '2017-06-18', 27, 0, 1159, 36, 5.83607, 6.75, 5.7907, 4.9773),
(2486, 'A Second Chance', 'Description Shoot anything you like, but your shutter speed must be exactly 1 second or it will be disqualified.', '2017-05-31', '2017-06-13', '2017-06-14', '2017-06-20', 38, 0, 1821, 63, 5.66337, 6.8163, 5.7083, 4.0),
(2487, 'Free Study 2017-06', 'Description Free Study for June, 2017.', '2017-06-01', '2017-06-30', '2017-07-01', '2017-07-07', 119, 0, 5894, 186, 5.48422, 7.3214, 5.45715, 3.8),
(2488, 'Alter Ego Diptych', 'Description Take two self-portraits depicting your normal self and your alter ego.', '2017-06-01', '2017-06-15', '2017-06-16', '2017-06-22', 14, 0, 621, 86, 6.38647, 7.4545, 6.2558, 5.6444),
(2489, 'Covfefe', 'Description The other day President Trump used the rather enigmatic non-word "covfefe" in one of his tweets. A few hours later he tweeted "Who can figure out the true meaning of ''covfefe''???" So let''s do it! Show us your best guess :-)', '2017-06-05', '2017-06-18', '2017-06-19', '2017-06-25', 37, 0, 2158, 112, 5.6798, 7.7414, 5.70595, 4.8421),
(2490, 'Lucky 7 VI', 'Description Take a photograph which contains exactly seven of the main subject.', '2017-06-07', '2017-06-20', '2017-06-21', '2017-06-27', 41, 0, 2077, 85, 5.6519, 6.9038, 5.4704, 4.6667),
(2491, 'Dirty Abstract', 'Description Make an abstract image that does not rely on clean lines or distinct patterns and shapes.', '2017-06-09', '2017-06-22', '2017-06-23', '2017-06-29', 47, 0, 2488, 106, 5.56833, 6.8519, 5.5608, 4.1346),
(2492, 'Landscape: Show us the Light!', 'Description The single trait most shared by great landscape/seascape photographers is their awareness of light and how it defines the scene. This is your week to show us you''ve got what it takes; capture an image of a landscape awash in luminosity, where the overriding sense the viewer takes from the shot is "Wow! What great light!"', '2017-06-12', '2017-06-25', '2017-06-26', '2017-07-02', 50, 0, 2657, 143, 5.85773, 7.7321, 5.8302, 4.1923),
(2493, 'Portrait From Behind II', 'Description Tell us something about your subject while shooting them from behind.', '2017-06-14', '2017-06-27', '2017-06-28', '2017-07-04', 65, 0, 4282, 198, 5.63638, 7.0725, 5.5111, 4.8),
(2494, 'Extended Free Study 2017-06', 'Description Extended Free Study for June, 2017.', '2017-06-15', '2017-07-14', '2017-07-15', '2017-07-21', 47, 0, 2261, 192, 5.88456, 7.0408, 5.90425, 4.7826),
(2495, 'Googly Eyes', 'Description Also known as Eyebombing. Let''s go have some fun this week and next :-)', '2017-06-16', '2017-06-29', '2017-06-30', '2017-07-06', 33, 0, 1497, 27, 5.63861, 6.5217, 5.6157, 3.9778),
(2496, 'Kitchen in B/W', 'Description Kitchens are fertile ground for photography. Stage a photograph OF, or IN, your kitchen. To make it tougher, do it in B/W. We intend "B/W" to include toned images such as sepia, selenium, cyanotype, etc.', '2017-06-19', '2017-07-02', '2017-07-03', '2017-07-09', 41, 0, 1939, 110, 5.49407, 6.766, 5.553, 3.8511),
(2497, 'Planes, Trains & Automobiles III', 'Description Photograph a mode of transportation  your options are restricted to planes, trains, and automobiles.', '2017-06-21', '2017-07-04', '2017-07-05', '2017-07-11', 42, 2, 2285, 103, 5.57243, 7.2679, 5.5492, 4.2545),
(2498, 'Red VI', 'Description Make your image a song of praise to the color red. Minimal editing: find it and snap it!', '2017-06-23', '2017-07-06', '2017-07-07', '2017-07-13', 42, 0, 2043, 167, 5.38424, 6.4694, 5.3542, 4.2245),
(2499, 'Beauty in Overwhelming Numbers', 'Description We can make extraordinary images sometimes by capturing the detail and beauty of simply masses and masses of something. Give it a try.', '2017-06-26', '2017-07-09', '2017-07-10', '2017-07-16', 44, 0, 2639, 162, 5.63433, 6.9839, 5.6066, 4.3667),
(2500, 'Improper White Balance', 'Description Sometimes using the WRONG white balance when shooting your image can produce an interesting effect. Give it a try in this MINIMAL EDITING challenge.', '2017-06-28', '2017-07-11', '2017-07-12', '2017-07-18', 36, 2, 2198, 139, 5.54732, 6.7619, 5.5711, 4.2787),
(2501, 'Comic Book Page', 'Description Put together something that looks like a single page of a comic book. It doesn''t need to be an existing comic book.', '2017-06-30', '2017-07-13', '2017-07-14', '2017-07-20', 21, 0, 1163, 83, 5.78332, 7.1481, 5.74105, 4.8929),
(2502, 'Free Study 2017-07', 'Description Free Study for July, 2017.', '2017-07-01', '2017-07-31', '2017-08-01', '2017-08-07', 120, 0, 7191, 290, 5.66277, 6.8846, 5.629, 4.5),
(2503, 'Loneliness', 'Description n/a', '2017-07-03', '2017-07-16', '2017-07-17', '2017-07-23', 60, 0, 3499, 177, 5.34781, 6.8276, 5.2241, 4.069),
(2504, 'Mucking About with Boats', 'Description Watercraft of all sorts encouraged :-)', '2017-07-05', '2017-07-18', '2017-07-19', '2017-07-25', 53, 0, 3408, 238, 5.6966, 7.2769, 5.62955, 4.3387),
(2505, 'Crop it TIGHT II', 'Description Your challenge this week is to go out and shoot an image that''s framed (or cropped) as tight as possible. You might crop down on some portion of a face, for example, or do a landscape shot that''s really up-close and tight, or a bug macro that''s just part of the bug, whatever works for you. Just get in close, then go a little tighter yet, and see what happens!', '2017-07-07', '2017-07-20', '2017-07-21', '2017-07-27', 74, 0, 3585, 183, 5.57517, 6.7115, 5.4898, 4.3111),
(2506, 'Out of Character', 'Description Take a photograph that''s as unlike your usual work as you can manage. Produce something you might honestly score as 6 or higher.', '2017-07-10', '2017-07-23', '2017-07-24', '2017-07-30', 48, 0, 2436, 174, 5.68966, 7.1321, 5.64, 4.549),
(2507, 'Hands II', 'Description Some are young, some are old - some are gnarled, some are supple - they all have character!', '2017-07-12', '2017-07-25', '2017-07-26', '2017-08-01', 56, 1, 3784, 169, 5.62791, 6.8986, 5.7227, 4.6364),
(2508, 'Before', 'Description Take a picture of something before it happens.', '2017-07-14', '2017-07-27', '2017-07-28', '2017-08-03', 48, 0, 2588, 118, 5.54598, 6.8113, 5.4727, 4.4444),
(2509, 'Extended Free Study 2017-07', 'Description Extended Free Study for July, 2017.', '2017-07-15', '2017-08-14', '2017-08-15', '2017-08-21', 46, 1, 1780, 181, 5.69775, 6.6923, 5.60735, 4.65),
(2510, 'Shapes VI', 'Description The shape of whatever you''re photographing should be the defining element in your composition.', '2017-07-17', '2017-07-30', '2017-07-31', '2017-08-06', 59, 0, 2945, 105, 5.60815, 6.9412, 5.66, 4.58),
(2511, 'Tools II', 'Description Tools: they''re what makes us human, and they''re everywhere. Show us some tools.', '2017-07-19', '2017-08-01', '2017-08-02', '2017-08-08', 34, 0, 2001, 77, 5.62569, 6.9333, 5.5345, 4.1695),
(2512, 'Hidden Gem VI  Mid-Term Quiz', 'Description It''s time for your 2017 Mid-Term Quiz: mine your 2017 archives-to-date for a picture you haven''t entered before that you''d really like to share :-) Your image must have been captured between 01-01-2017 and the closing date of this challenge.', '2017-07-21', '2017-08-03', '2017-08-04', '2017-08-10', 102, 2, 6172, 432, 5.71387, 6.8167, 5.6835, 4.1148),
(2513, 'Celebrating Magnum''s 70th Birthday', 'Description The Magnum agency is celebrating its 70th birthday this year. To honor this most influential of all photo agencies, here is your challenge: Take an image in the style of your favorite living Magnum photographer. We have chosen "living" so this doesn''t turn into a Cartier-Bresson challenge :-) The title of your image should simply be the name of the photographer you are honoring.', '2017-07-23', '2017-08-06', '2017-08-07', '2017-08-13', 38, 0, 1494, 52, 5.68675, 6.5, 5.6154, 5.0769),
(2514, 'Leading Lines VIII', 'Description In photography, leading lines are used to draw the viewer into (or occasionally even out of) your photograph. Google the topic, then practice what you learned :-)', '2017-07-26', '2017-08-08', '2017-08-09', '2017-08-15', 59, 0, 3621, 200, 5.64761, 6.9508, 5.664, 4.1803),
(2515, 'Negative Image IV', 'Description Capture an image that works well when inverted, via post processing, into a negative.', '2017-07-28', '2017-08-10', '2017-08-11', '2017-08-17', 59, 2, 2916, 141, 5.53944, 6.449, 5.5294, 4.36),
(2516, 'Original Artwork', 'Description You can''t google for ideas on this one. Let your creativity run wild. Take and/or make the most original-looking, non-derivative image that you possibly can.', '2017-07-31', '2017-08-13', '2017-08-14', '2017-08-20', 40, 1, 2048, 277, 5.79395, 6.7115, 5.7048, 4.902),
(2517, 'Free Study 2017-08', 'Description Free Study for August, 2017.', '2017-08-01', '2017-08-31', '2017-09-01', '2017-09-07', 119, 1, 7644, 375, 5.68721, 7.0, 5.7544, 4.3226),
(2518, 'Jimmy Buffet Song/Lyrics', 'Description Choose a line or title from a Jimmy Buffet song and make it come to life in a photograph. The song title or lyric MUST be the title of your image.', '2017-08-02', '2017-08-15', '2017-08-16', '2017-08-22', 36, 0, 1649, 122, 5.81079, 6.9149, 5.8696, 4.7826),
(2519, 'Science Fiction Novel Cover', 'Description It doesn''t have to be an actual, published SF novel; you can just make one up.', '2017-08-04', '2017-08-17', '2017-08-18', '2017-08-24', 32, 0, 1508, 123, 5.90385, 7.3542, 5.875, 4.8125),
(2520, 'Show Us Your Morning', 'Description Take a photo between 5 AM and 11 AM in your time zone. Get up and out there, or stay in bed, either way, take a picture of it in some gorgeous morning light.', '2017-08-07', '2017-08-20', '2017-08-21', '2017-08-27', 56, 0, 3001, 218, 5.83739, 7.3704, 5.9273, 4.5472),
(2521, 'Farm Animals', 'Description Farm animals in/on their farm, ranch, pasture, paddock, wherever they belong.', '2017-08-09', '2017-08-22', '2017-08-23', '2017-08-29', 38, 0, 2482, 203, 5.8062, 7.4545, 5.9394, 4.4308),
(2522, 'Playgrounds', 'Description Literally, "places where you play". Kids have ''em, grownups have ''em. Show us a playground.', '2017-08-11', '2017-08-24', '2017-08-25', '2017-08-31', 33, 0, 1969, 172, 5.68614, 7.1148, 5.5763, 4.2373),
(2523, 'Grown-Up Toys', 'Description You may have started with dolls and blocks, but what do you play with NOW?', '2017-08-14', '2017-08-27', '2017-08-28', '2017-09-03', 43, 0, 2660, 141, 5.71504, 7.1746, 5.7265, 4.4918),
(2524, 'Extended Free Study 2017-08', 'Description Extended Free Study for August, 2017.', '2017-08-15', '2017-09-14', '2017-09-15', '2017-09-21', 47, 0, 1858, 103, 5.64909, 6.475, 5.6327, 4.75),
(2525, 'Lens Effects', 'Description This is a minimal editing challenge where the entry should demonstrate some interesting lens effects... this could cover specialist lenses such as Lensbaby as well as techniques such as free lensing... the aim of the challenge and minimal editing rule is to see what can be achieved straight from the camera without post-processing distortions...', '2017-08-16', '2017-08-29', '2017-08-30', '2017-09-05', 45, 2, 2672, 208, 5.50861, 6.6349, 5.54835, 4.5574),
(2526, 'Fruits & Vegetables III', 'Description Photograph a fruit. Photograph a vegetable. Photograph a fruit and a vegetable together. Photograph as few or as many of each as you like.', '2017-08-18', '2017-08-31', '2017-09-01', '2017-09-07', 43, 0, 1905, 113, 5.54278, 6.6889, 5.4482, 4.2955),
(2527, 'Solar Eclipse 2017', 'Description August 21st offers a rare, total solar eclipse across a wide swath of North America, and even more folks will see it as 75% to 65% partial. This is a challenge for the eclipse-heads among us. Have at it, guys and gals!', '2017-08-19', '2017-08-28', '2017-08-29', '2017-09-04', 44, 0, 3008, 96, 5.85771, 7.0725, 5.75, 4.4478),
(2528, 'Beds & Sofas & Chairs', 'Description Use a bed/beds and/or a sofa/sofas and/or a chair/chairs as the subject of or as the context for your composition.', '2017-08-21', '2017-09-03', '2017-09-04', '2017-09-10', 46, 0, 2247, 157, 5.68847, 6.7143, 5.64, 4.6122),
(2529, 'Reflections without Mirrors VII', 'Description Creatively photograph a reflecting surface that is not a mirror while keeping your camera out of the shot.', '2017-08-23', '2017-09-05', '2017-09-06', '2017-09-12', 56, 0, 3672, 189, 5.70289, 7.3281, 5.7692, 3.8154),
(2530, 'Cubism', 'Description Cubism was a 20th-century avant-garde artistic movement that revolutionized the art world. Painters such as Pablo Picasso, Fernand Léger, Georges Braque and Juan Gris embraced this new artistic sensibility. Create your own cubist photograph.', '2017-08-25', '2017-09-07', '2017-09-08', '2017-09-14', 38, 0, 1707, 84, 5.62742, 7.1556, 5.5227, 4.3778),
(2531, 'Candid IX', 'Description Get up close & personal: capture a candid moment.', '2017-08-28', '2017-09-10', '2017-09-11', '2017-09-17', 57, 0, 2909, 197, 5.6693, 7.1373, 5.6989, 4.2941),
(2532, 'Emotive Architecture II', 'Description Take a picture of a structure in a way that emphasizes emotional content rather than form. Your subject should be identifiable as a structure, and although human elements can appear in the image, it should be predominantly about the structure itself.', '2017-08-30', '2017-09-12', '2017-09-13', '2017-09-19', 48, 0, 2851, 122, 5.76149, 7.0323, 5.8475, 4.1356),
(2533, 'Free Study 2017-09', 'Description Free Study for September, 2017.', '2017-09-01', '2017-09-30', '2017-10-01', '2017-10-07', 119, 0, 7126, 250, 5.69787, 7.0308, 5.66655, 4.4516),
(2534, 'A Single Tree III', 'Description Take a photo where a single tree is the main subject.', '2017-09-01', '2017-09-14', '2017-09-15', '2017-09-21', 38, 0, 1800, 96, 5.32667, 6.8776, 5.3191, 3.7872),
(2535, 'Rocks, Stones, Pebbles II', 'Description Smardaz found a big one last week; see what YOU can come up with :-)', '2017-09-04', '2017-09-17', '2017-09-18', '2017-09-24', 39, 0, 2152, 102, 5.58457, 6.8, 5.6576, 3.8519),
(2536, 'Room Interiors', 'Description N/A', '2017-09-06', '2017-09-19', '2017-09-20', '2017-09-26', 39, 0, 2327, 36, 5.65191, 6.85, 5.6694, 4.0984),
(2538, 'Weather II', 'Description Go out and photograph the weather OR the effects weather can have on the environment.', '2017-09-08', '2017-09-21', '2017-09-22', '2017-09-28', 39, 0, 1960, 92, 5.9051, 7.14, 6.0098, 4.46),
(2539, 'A Part of A Thing', 'Description We can often find the heart or essence of a thing more in its parts or its details than in the whole. Go shoot with that in mind. This is not meant to be a "macro" challenge...', '2017-09-11', '2017-09-24', '2017-09-25', '2017-10-01', 51, 0, 2594, 131, 5.60756, 6.2708, 5.63, 4.72),
(2540, 'Shallow DOF VIII', 'Description Shallow DOF is a valuable tool for isolating your subject and it can be used to convey significant emotional context in portraiture and otherwise. For this challenge, use shallow DOF thoughtfully and purposefully :-)', '2017-09-13', '2017-09-26', '2017-09-27', '2017-10-03', 66, 1, 3828, 177, 5.40778, 7.3167, 5.3684, 3.8621),
(2541, 'People at their Jobs', 'Description Show us a person or people at work doing their jobs.', '2017-09-15', '2017-09-28', '2017-09-29', '2017-10-05', 34, 0, 1813, 72, 5.70546, 7.1887, 5.7593, 4.1481),
(2542, 'Extended Free Study 2017-09', 'Description Extended Free Study for September, 2017.', '2017-09-15', '2017-10-14', '2017-10-15', '2017-10-21', 52, 0, 2249, 161, 5.70253, 6.9773, 5.7727, 4.5476),
(2543, 'Dada  The Art Movement', 'Description Dada (or Dadaism) was an art movement of the European avant-garde in the early 20th century. Developed in reaction to World War I, the Dada movement consisted of artists who rejected the logic, reason, and aestheticism of modern capitalist society, instead expressing nonsense, irrationality, and anti-bourgeois protest in their works. Create a dada-rific photograph.', '2017-09-18', '2017-10-01', '2017-10-02', '2017-10-08', 40, 1, 1578, 107, 5.77947, 6.5952, 5.82715, 4.8),
(2544, 'Books II', 'Description OF books. Or ABOUT books. Or RELATED to books. Or any combination thereof.', '2017-09-20', '2017-10-03', '2017-10-04', '2017-10-10', 46, 0, 2464, 93, 5.50325, 7.1698, 5.4423, 3.9434),
(2545, 'Tall!!!', 'Description N/A', '2017-09-22', '2017-10-05', '2017-10-06', '2017-10-12', 35, 0, 1736, 111, 5.79147, 7.42, 5.74255, 4.7551),
(2546, 'Waterscape', 'Description We do a lot of landscapes in DPC; let''s try a waterscape! Seascape, Riverscape, Lakescape, Puddlescape, Creekscape, Pondscape, whatever...', '2017-09-25', '2017-10-08', '2017-10-09', '2017-10-15', 66, 1, 3525, 57, 5.60255, 7.1887, 5.5849, 3.9057),
(2547, 'Quiet II', 'Description Seek out moments of serenity and contemplation amidst the clamor of the turning year.', '2017-09-27', '2017-10-10', '2017-10-11', '2017-10-17', 66, 0, 3629, 123, 5.64233, 6.8, 5.5893, 4.5),
(2548, '!deppilF', 'Description Take a photo that makes creative use of being flipped backwards or upside down.', '2017-09-29', '2017-10-12', '2017-10-13', '2017-10-19', 41, 0, 1669, 63, 5.74356, 6.8537, 5.6951, 4.925),
(2549, 'Free Study 2017-10', 'Description Free Study for October, 2017.', '2017-10-01', '2017-10-31', '2017-11-01', '2017-11-07', 111, 0, 6362, 342, 5.79566, 7.0893, 5.8121, 4.5965),
(2550, 'Bite Me', 'Description Open to interpretation... whether you feel testy, tasty or long in the tooth.', '2017-10-02', '2017-10-15', '2017-10-16', '2017-10-22', 41, 0, 1666, 63, 5.63986, 6.95, 5.62955, 4.4634),
