(2832, 'Photographing Photographers II', 'Description Take a unique photograph of someone else taking a photograph. In other words, NO SELFIES! (Photographs of others taking selfies are fair game.)', '2019-04-05', '2019-04-18', '2019-04-19', '2019-04-25', 22, 1, 972, 52, 5.45267, 6.4773, 5.3556, 4.6744),
(2833, 'You Name It III', 'Description Ever had trouble coming up with a good title? Just title your entry "You Name It!" sit back, and relax: Voters will have the fun of suggesting good titles in their comments. This is a time for challenge participants and voters to have some good, clean fun.', '2019-04-08', '2019-04-21', '2019-04-22', '2019-04-28', 48, 0, 2346, 1686, 5.91006, 7.0204, 5.84, 4.9796),
(2834, 'Fiction', 'Description "Fiction", for this challenge, is defined as: N: An imaginative creation or a pretense that does not represent actuality but has been invented.', '2019-04-10', '2019-04-23', '2019-04-24', '2019-04-30', 35, 0, 1490, 50, 5.69329, 7.119, 5.596, 4.6098),
(2835, 'High Key IV', 'Description N/A', '2019-04-12', '2019-04-25', '2019-04-26', '2019-05-02', 39, 0, 1714, 79, 5.59102, 7.0, 5.60235, 4.4091),
(2836, 'The Springing of the Year (Archival)', 'Description Dip into your archives and find an image that sings "Spring!" Here''s a poem from Frost to get you going: Prayer in Springtime Oh, give us pleasure in the flowers to-day; And give us not to think so far away As the uncertain harvest; keep us here All simply in the springing of the year. Oh, give us pleasure in the orchard white, Like nothing else by day, like ghosts by night; And make us happy in the happy bees, The swarm dilating round the perfect trees. And make us happy in the darting bird That suddenly above the bees is heard, The meteor that thrusts in with needle bill, And off a blossom in mid air stands still. For this is love and nothing else is love, The which it is reserved for God above To sanctify to what far ends He will, But which it only needs that we fulfill.', '2019-04-15', '2019-04-28', '2019-04-29', '2019-05-05', 55, 0, 2664, 111, 5.86749, 6.7959, 5.92685, 5.0851),
(2837, 'Extended Free Study 2019-04', 'Description Extended Free Study for April, 2019.', '2019-04-15', '2019-05-14', '2019-05-15', '2019-05-21', 43, 0, 1816, 65, 5.80672, 7.1395, 5.8469, 4.6512),
(2838, 'Regret(s)', 'Description Maybe you have ''em, maybe you don''t: show us!', '2019-04-17', '2019-04-30', '2019-05-01', '2019-05-07', 35, 1, 1358, 55, 5.4838, 6.3846, 5.4231, 4.8462),
(2839, 'Duct Tape', 'Description Use duct tape one way or another in your photograph.', '2019-04-19', '2019-05-02', '2019-05-03', '2019-05-09', 15, 0, 650, 98, 5.68462, 6.7273, 5.81395, 4.4884),
(2840, 'Windows (the glass kind) II', 'Description This week it''s windows. Windows in buildings, cars, boats, trains, planes, the kind you can look through. Make ''em shine!', '2019-04-22', '2019-05-05', '2019-05-06', '2019-05-12', 29, 1, 1098, 118, 5.64845, 6.5263, 5.6316, 5.027),
(2841, 'Avant-Garde', 'Description Avant-garde represents a pushing of the boundaries of what is accepted as the norm or the status quo. Do so with your photography this week. Show us cutting edge in subject and/or technique and/or style.', '2019-04-24', '2019-05-07', '2019-05-08', '2019-05-14', 38, 0, 1649, 116, 5.58763, 6.5778, 5.5455, 4.5227),
