(2895, 'Rat''s-Eye Perspective', 'Description For this one go low-level down to close to the street/ground where the rats hang out and then take a photograph from that point of view. Keep in mind that rats always skulk around the corners/edges of the street or houses or trees: you never see them taking a short-cut through busy or open spaces.', '2019-08-12', '2019-08-25', '2019-08-26', '2019-09-01', 29, 1, 1178, 113, 5.83192, 7.1667, 5.72895, 4.65),
(2896, 'Book Cover II', 'Description Invent a fake book of any genre (novel, biography, textbook, anything) and show us the cover.', '2019-08-14', '2019-08-27', '2019-08-28', '2019-09-03', 26, 1, 1124, 143, 5.93772, 7.0238, 5.8864, 5.0465),
(2897, 'Extended Free Study 2019-08', 'Description Extended Free Study for August, 2019.', '2019-08-15', '2019-09-14', '2019-09-15', '2019-09-21', 47, 0, 1656, 19, 5.875, 7.2857, 5.81665, 4.5556),
(2898, 'Boats IV', 'Description Big boats, little boats, shiny boats, wrecked boats, workboats, playboats, powerboats, sailboats, rowboats, paper boats, duck boats, swan boats, ferryboats, BOATS!', '2019-08-16', '2019-08-29', '2019-08-30', '2019-09-05', 36, 0, 1679, 110, 5.81239, 7.3913, 5.7391, 4.1778),
(2899, 'Landscape VIII', 'Description A landscape doesn''t have to be dramatic to be memorable. Meadows, fields, streams, rivers, lakes, oceans, mountains, deserts... we all have landscapes around us, and success comes from the light :-)', '2019-08-19', '2019-09-01', '2019-09-02', '2019-09-08', 48, 0, 2314, 62, 5.85177, 7.8723, 5.7083, 4.6042),
(2900, '240 Pixels', 'Description Some scenes lend themselves to a high-aspect-ratio crop. Show us something that does. This was first run as "160 Pixels" but now we have gone from 800px to 1200px, hence the 240px to maintain the ratio.', '2019-08-21', '2019-09-03', '2019-09-04', '2019-09-10', 55, 3, 3013, 94, 5.87488, 7.569, 5.8609, 4.0179),
(2901, 'Surface', 'Description As photographers, we tend to be involved with the photography of THINGS, be they people or objects or landscapes, whatever. But how often do we concentrate on the SURFACES of things? For this challenge, do that :-)', '2019-08-23', '2019-09-05', '2019-09-06', '2019-09-12', 48, 1, 2082, 33, 5.60279, 6.6818, 5.5227, 4.4773),
(2902, 'Parts II', 'Description Photograph ''part'' of something. Do not photograph the entire subject. Be creative with your angle and approach to your subject.', '2019-08-26', '2019-09-08', '2019-09-09', '2019-09-15', 57, 1, 2420, 86, 5.82025, 7.3488, 5.74415, 4.8571),
(2903, 'Five & Yellow', 'Description It''s what you make of it... Have fun!', '2019-08-28', '2019-09-10', '2019-09-11', '2019-09-17', 43, 0, 2467, 65, 5.4467, 6.7458, 5.4823, 3.6842),
(2904, 'Balancing Flash Outdoors', 'Description Most of us have on-camera flashes that can be triggered to flash in daylight, not just automatically. Some of us have dedicated external flashes/strobes that can do this as well. But it seems as if, in these days of HDR and Extreme PS, balancing light outdoors with what used to be called "fill flash" is something of a lost art. SO... Give it a try yourself, There are many tutorials available online.', '2019-08-30', '2019-09-12', '2019-09-13', '2019-09-19', 18, 0, 929, 42, 5.77933, 7.0962, 5.75, 4.1176),
(2905, 'Free Study 2019-09', 'Description Free Study for September, 2019.', '2019-09-01', '2019-09-30', '2019-10-01', '2019-10-07', 68, 1, 3186, 126, 5.78939, 7.4783, 5.7872, 4.6383),
(2906, 'Aftermath II', 'Description Title your image "Aftermath", and shoot to fit the title.', '2019-09-02', '2019-09-15', '2019-09-16', '2019-09-22', 37, 1, 1605, 63, 5.63614, 6.7907, 5.5867, 4.7045),
(2907, 'The Neighborhood', 'Description N/A', '2019-09-04', '2019-09-17', '2019-09-18', '2019-09-24', 40, 0, 2032, 33, 5.60925, 7.08, 5.58, 4.4615),
(2908, 'Human Faces from/in the Non-Human', 'Description Create a human face or faces out of, or find them in, non-human material.', '2019-09-06', '2019-09-19', '2019-09-20', '2019-09-26', 27, 0, 1229, 46, 5.57852, 6.766, 5.53815, 4.0667),
(2909, 'Round II', 'Description Show us roundness, however you choose to express it.', '2019-09-09', '2019-09-22', '2019-09-23', '2019-09-29', 46, 0, 2028, 61, 5.72535, 6.7273, 5.6512, 4.6591),
(2910, 'Robert Frank: A Homage', 'Description Robert Frank, who died on Monday at the age of 94, looked at the country through the critical eyes of an outsider. Originally from Switzerland, he travelled across the United States taking photos of factory workers, prostitutes, cross-dressers, cowboys and Americans of all stripes. He rarely spoke to his subjects, but possessed an uncanny ability to capture the alienation, poverty and racism that rippled throughout his adopted homeland. Franks 1958 book The Americans, which assembled 83 photos taken during his cross-country tour, had a profound impact on the art of photography [and] changed the course of American photography, says Sarah Greenough, senior curator and head of the department of photographs at the National Gallery of Art. Blurb courtesy of "Smithsonian"', '2019-09-11', '2019-09-24', '2019-09-25', '2019-10-01', 29, 0, 1378, 36, 5.83019, 6.625, 5.8646, 4.3913),
(2911, 'Square Crop VI', 'Description N/A', '2019-09-13', '2019-09-26', '2019-09-27', '2019-10-03', 54, 1, 2258, 39, 5.82152, 6.8537, 5.7442, 4.9286),
(2912, 'Extended Free Study 2019-09', 'Description Extended Free Study for September, 2019.', '2019-09-15', '2019-10-14', '2019-10-15', '2019-10-21', 42, 0, 1412, 111, 5.91218, 6.9091, 5.9412, 4.7647),
(2913, 'As Seen at the Museum', 'Description Show us a museum, or whatever''s IN the museum.', '2019-09-16', '2019-09-29', '2019-09-30', '2019-10-06', 24, 1, 992, 40, 5.62198, 7.0238, 5.561, 4.6098),
(2914, 'Separation II', 'Description Your challenge this week is to capture the idea of separation in a picture.', '2019-09-18', '2019-10-01', '2019-10-02', '2019-10-08', 40, 0, 1771, 19, 5.50085, 7.0233, 5.4565, 3.75),
(2915, 'Rocks, Stones, Pebbles III (Archival)', 'Description Thinking about Wynn Bullock today: "Not form rock, not object rock, but the light that IS the rock."', '2019-09-20', '2019-10-03', '2019-10-04', '2019-10-10', 56, 0, 2383, 32, 5.85061, 7.119, 5.8333, 4.6047),
(2916, 'Brown II', 'Description Let''s face it; "brown" is arguably the least-appreciated color of them all. But every color deserves its day: this week, it''s brown''s turn to bask in the limelight.', '2019-09-23', '2019-10-06', '2019-10-07', '2019-10-13', 43, 0, 1841, 30, 5.63227, 6.5238, 5.6047, 4.5909),
(2917, 'Film Noir III', 'Description "Film Noir" is a genre of film between 1940 and 1960, originating in the United States, employing heavy shadows and patterns of darkness, in which the protagonist dies, meets defeat, or achieves meaningless victory in the end. Take a photo in the style of or reminiscent of film noir.', '2019-09-25', '2019-10-08', '2019-10-09', '2019-10-15', 36, 0, 1975, 38, 5.65671, 7.9107, 5.5714, 3.1346),
