(3243, 'Leading Lines X (ARCHIVAL)', 'Description In photography, leading lines are used to draw the viewer into (or occasionally even out of) your photograph. Google the topic, then practice what you learned :-)', '2021-06-16', '2021-06-29', '2021-06-30', '2021-07-06', 42, 0, 1465, 6, 5.68805, 7.1081, 5.6571, 4.6),
(3244, 'Late', 'Description N/A', '2021-06-18', '2021-07-01', '2021-07-02', '2021-07-08', 17, 0, 441, 17, 5.59864, 6.52, 5.6869, 4.6538),
(3245, 'Word for Word', 'Description It''s time to get literal, folks! Your challenge this week is very specific  Choose a song/book/movie title that includes at least two "things", and make a photograph that specifically includes each "thing" in the title. For example, you might illustrate "The Breakfast Club" with a shot of a golf club protruding from a bowl of cereal. Or perhaps "Planes, Trains, and Automobiles" with a shot that includes all three. Sounds simple, right? Go for it! Your image MUST be titled with ONLY the title of the work you are referencing.', '2021-06-21', '2021-07-04', '2021-07-05', '2021-07-11', 22, 0, 580, 24, 5.75517, 6.8519, 5.6923, 5.0741),
(3246, 'Places Where Food is Grown & Harvested (ARCHIVAL)', 'Description Everything from windowsill herb gardens up to backyard plots, fish farms, rice paddies, vast fields of corn, you get the idea.', '2021-06-23', '2021-07-06', '2021-07-07', '2021-07-13', 33, 0, 1080, 14, 5.72315, 7.0, 5.7273, 4.0),
