(3734, 'Billboard II', 'Take a photograph that might grace a highway billboard (those large signs you see on the side of the road). Your submission should be in landscape orientation, and should be twice as wide as it is tall to simulate a common billboard aspect ratio. Title your entry with what the billboard would be promoting.', '2024-02-12', '2024-02-25', '2024-02-26', '2024-03-03', 16, 0, 442, 32, 6.16516, 7.5, 5.9259, 5.1429),
(3735, 'Doors, Gates, Knobs, Locks & Handles III', 'N/A', '2024-02-14', '2024-02-27', '2024-02-28', '2024-03-05', 24, 0, 730, 35, 5.68219, 6.7742, 5.6129, 4.7742),
(3736, 'Extended Free Study 2024-02', 'Extended Free Study for February, 2024.', '2024-02-15', '2024-03-14', '2024-03-15', '2024-03-21', 30, 0, 715, 10, 5.95804, 7.0, 5.9167, 4.875),
(3737, 'Macro XII', 'N/A', '2024-02-16', '2024-02-29', '2024-03-01', '2024-03-07', 18, 0, 367, 8, 6.22343, 7.2, 6.1905, 4.7143),
(3738, 'Hidden Gem VII', 'Dig through your archives to show us the best photo you''ve taken with a digital camera that you haven''t already entered in a challenge. Make sure you still have the original with valid EXIF in case it''s needed for validation.', '2024-02-19', '2024-03-03', '2024-03-04', '2024-03-10', 40, 0, 1176, 27, 6.1233, 7.2759, 6.1034, 4.1724),
(3739, 'Despair III', 'Consider the underlying thought that a photograph is about communication and that the best photographs should have something to say other than ''wooh, pretty''. In the spirit of this thought, capture your best communication of despair.', '2024-02-21', '2024-03-05', '2024-03-06', '2024-03-12', 19, 0, 523, 13, 5.29254, 7.1786, 5.1085, 4.4444),
(3740, 'Forced Perspective III', 'Forced perspective is a technique that employs optical illusion to make an object appear farther away, closer, larger, or smaller than it actually is. It is used primarily in photography, filmmaking, and architecture.', '2024-02-23', '2024-03-07', '2024-03-08', '2024-03-14', 12, 0, 251, 11, 5.91633, 7.5909, 5.8095, 4.7727),
(3741, 'Photojournalism V', 'Put yourself in the shoes of a magazine or newspaper photographer and try to capture a shot worthy of the front page.', '2024-02-26', '2024-03-10', '2024-03-11', '2024-03-17', 13, 0, 306, 15, 5.7451, 6.125, 5.8696, 4.8261),
(3742, 'Steampunk II', 'Photograph a Steampunk-inspired scene.', '2024-02-28', '2024-03-12', '2024-03-13', '2024-03-19', 8, 0, 235, 13, 5.87234, 7.5, 5.5, 4.2069),
(3743, 'Diagonal III', 'Most of us tend to default to compositions that are oriented around strong horizontal or vertical axes. Your challenge this week is to incorporate a diagonal axis as the major compositional thrust of your image. Note that this does NOT require the presence of a diagonal "line".', '2024-03-01', '2024-03-14', '2024-03-15', '2024-03-21', 30, 0, 676, 11, 5.72929, 6.913, 5.5455, 4.8636),
(3744, 'Free Study 2024-03', 'Free Study for March, 2024.', '2024-03-01', '2024-03-31', '2024-04-01', '2024-04-07', 40, 0, 1122, 16, 6.02852, 7.3571, 5.9286, 4.75),
(3745, '7 Deadly Sins IV', 'Pride, Greed, Envy, Wrath, Lust, Gluttony, Sloth. Represent one or more in a photograph.', '2024-03-04', '2024-03-17', '2024-03-18', '2024-03-24', 18, 0, 403, 19, 5.62531, 6.9565, 5.4545, 4.6818),
(3746, 'Grown-Up Toys II', 'You may have started with dolls and blocks, but what do you play with NOW?', '2024-03-06', '2024-03-19', '2024-03-20', '2024-03-26', 24, 0, 727, 10, 5.66988, 6.7586, 5.9333, 4.1613),
(3747, 'On The Edge II', 'There are many boundaries in our world. Create a photograph that speaks to these transitions, borders, edges.', '2024-03-08', '2024-03-21', '2024-03-22', '2024-03-28', 17, 0, 452, 15, 5.72124, 6.7778, 5.73935, 4.5769),
(3748, 'Intimacy II', 'Create a photo that somehow communicates the concept of "intimacy."', '2024-03-11', '2024-03-24', '2024-03-25', '2024-03-31', 12, 0, 317, 16, 6.19243, 6.9615, 6.3462, 5.1154),
(3749, 'Pi(e) Day III', 'π : It''s International Pi Day tomorrow, 03/14!', '2024-03-13', '2024-03-26', '2024-03-27', '2024-04-02', 14, 1, 395, 14, 5.33671, 6.5161, 5.3801, 3.8214),
(3750, 'Minimalism VIII', 'N/A', '2024-03-15', '2024-03-28', '2024-03-29', '2024-04-04', 24, 1, 713, 16, 5.77419, 6.8, 5.8333, 4.6897),
(3751, 'Extended Free Study 2024-03', 'Extended Free Study for March, 2024.', '2024-03-15', '2024-04-14', '2024-04-15', '2024-04-21', 30, 0, 706, 39, 6.04957, 6.913, 6.1304, 4.5417),
