(3808, 'Serpentine II', 'ADJECTIVE 1. Of or like a serpent or snake. "serpentine coils" NOUN 1. A dark green mineral consisting of hydrated magnesium silicate, sometimes mottled or spotted like a snake''s skin. 2. A thing in the shape of a winding curve or line, in particular. VERB 1. Move or lie in a winding path or line. "Fresh tire tracks serpentined back toward the hopper"', '2024-07-05', '2024-07-18', '2024-07-19', '2024-07-25', 15, 0, 276, 6, 6.46377, 8.0, 6.2734, 4.7895),
(3809, 'Tall!!! II', 'N/A', '2024-07-08', '2024-07-21', '2024-07-22', '2024-07-28', 20, 0, 447, 17, 5.94183, 7.0909, 5.9091, 5.0435),
(3810, 'Rule of Thirds X', 'Study up on the "rule of thirds" and use it to inform your composition.', '2024-07-10', '2024-07-23', '2024-07-24', '2024-07-30', 26, 0, 584, 9, 5.90925, 7.0909, 5.9091, 4.7391),
(3811, 'Red IX', 'Make your image a song of praise to the color red. Minimal editing: find it and snap it!', '2024-07-12', '2024-07-25', '2024-07-26', '2024-08-01', 24, 0, 495, 13, 5.93131, 6.6, 6.0, 5.0952),
(3812, 'Abstract IV', 'Think of "abstraction" as a concept: we think of "abstract art" as non-representational images nowadays, but the core of abstraction is to derive the essence from the thing FROM the thing itself. For examples of that in art, look no further than the early 20th-century abstractionists. In any case, THINK about it :-)', '2024-07-15', '2024-07-28', '2024-07-29', '2024-08-04', 27, 0, 594, 30, 6.04209, 7.4091, 6.06925, 4.9545),
(3813, 'Circle VII', 'Take a photograph where this basic shape is a key element (or elements) in your composition.', '2024-07-17', '2024-07-30', '2024-07-31', '2024-08-06', 27, 1, 645, 9, 5.7845, 6.88, 5.67335, 4.4583),
(3814, 'Extended Free Study 2024-07', 'Extended Free Study for July, 2024.', '2024-07-15', '2024-08-14', '2024-08-15', '2024-08-21', 27, 0, 574, 49, 6.09582, 7.6667, 5.95455, 4.7143),
(3815, 'Proportion III', 'Make an image that conveys proportion or the lack thereof.', '2024-07-19', '2024-08-01', '2024-08-02', '2024-08-08', 15, 0, 328, 15, 6.15244, 7.2727, 6.2067, 5.2174),
(3816, 'Skyscape IV', 'Make the sky the subject of your photo this week; if the landscape plays any role it all, have it be a supporting role.', '2024-07-22', '2024-08-04', '2024-08-05', '2024-08-11', 22, 0, 507, 25, 5.90927, 6.7917, 5.8696, 3.8571),
(3817, 'Make it Square IV', 'Find or compose a scene that suits a square framing. Your image must be cropped to a perfect square. If it isn''t, it''s a DQ.', '2024-07-24', '2024-08-06', '2024-08-07', '2024-08-13', 30, 0, 776, 21, 6.0683, 7.1923, 6.0, 4.9615),
(3818, 'Point, Pointer, Pointed, Pointless', 'I need some pointers on scheduling. What''s the point of this challenge, anyway? Pointed responses welcome. Maybe it''s a pointless exercise? Whatever. You MUST use some form of the word "point" in your title (Or what would be the point)?', '2024-07-26', '2024-08-08', '2024-08-09', '2024-08-15', 22, 0, 412, 7, 5.79854, 6.6316, 5.7778, 5.2632),
(3819, 'Vegetable/Split', 'Take a vegetable, any vegetable and cut it open. Show us what it''s like inside. Pay particular attention to the light.', '2024-07-29', '2024-08-11', '2024-08-12', '2024-08-18', 18, 0, 475, 44, 6.17474, 7.3077, 6.1111, 5.0385),
(3820, 'Long Exposure X', 'Long exposures can often create very dramatic effects in photography. Use a longer than normal exposure to create the impact of your image.', '2024-07-31', '2024-08-13', '2024-08-14', '2024-08-20', 19, 1, 616, 33, 6.14935, 7.6364, 6.12215, 5.125),
(3821, 'Free Study 2024-08', 'Free Study for August, 2024.', '2024-08-01', '2024-08-31', '2024-09-01', '2024-09-07', 44, 0, 904, 13, 5.98009, 7.55, 5.9, 4.6842),
(3822, 'Impressionism V', 'Learn about the techniques of impressionism, and incorporate them into a photograph.', '2024-08-02', '2024-08-15', '2024-08-16', '2024-08-22', 19, 0, 444, 37, 5.76577, 6.913, 5.95655, 4.1667),
(3823, 'Personification V', 'Personification occurs when inanimate objects are endowed with human qualities or represented as possessing human form or personality. Take a photo of something non-human that still shows human characteristics or evokes a human feeling.', '2024-08-05', '2024-08-18', '2024-08-19', '2024-08-25', 17, 0, 412, 9, 5.8835, 6.9583, 5.875, 4.4783),
(3824, 'Rocks, Paper, Scissors III', 'Your photograph must contain one or more of these items.', '2024-08-07', '2024-08-20', '2024-08-21', '2024-08-27', 22, 0, 556, 12, 5.6205, 6.6, 5.5385, 4.68),
(3825, 'Structures at Night II', 'Take a picture of an artificial structure (or structures) at night.', '2024-08-09', '2024-08-22', '2024-08-23', '2024-08-29', 18, 0, 401, 11, 5.95511, 7.2727, 6.0435, 4.0476),
(3826, 'Store or Shop Interiors', 'Take us inside places where things are sold.', '2024-08-12', '2024-08-25', '2024-08-26', '2024-09-01', 19, 0, 426, 9, 5.53756, 6.4783, 5.55535, 4.913),
(3827, 'Long Shadows II', 'N/A', '2024-08-14', '2024-08-27', '2024-08-28', '2024-09-03', 17, 1, 452, 39, 5.92478, 8.0385, 5.64105, 5.037),
(3828, 'Extended Free Study 2024-08', 'Extended Free Study for August, 2024.', '2024-08-15', '2024-09-14', '2024-09-15', '2024-09-21', 32, 0, 622, 23, 5.99839, 7.5789, 5.9474, 4.9474),
(3829, 'Human Portrait, Head and Shoulders II', 'Let''s keep it classic, let''s keep it simple, and let''s do it really well: the "head & shoulders" portrait is a staple of the craft of photography.', '2024-08-16', '2024-08-29', '2024-08-30', '2024-09-05', 15, 0, 424, 17, 5.87972, 6.7241, 5.9107, 5.0),
(3830, 'Underneath', 'Flip it over or get beneath and show us the part we don''t usually see.', '2024-08-19', '2024-09-01', '2024-09-02', '2024-09-08', 20, 0, 448, 26, 5.875, 6.7826, 5.7391, 4.7143),
(3831, 'Post-It Note II', 'Creatively use 1 or more post-it notes (or any brand of self-sticking notes) in your entry.', '2024-08-21', '2024-09-03', '2024-09-04', '2024-09-10', 9, 0, 211, 25, 6.18009, 6.7391, 6.21195, 5.5417),
(3832, 'Tools of the Trade III', 'Photograph the tools specific to a certain trade/job. Include the job/trade in your title, please.', '2024-08-23', '2024-09-05', '2024-09-06', '2024-09-12', 13, 0, 343, 22, 5.87172, 7.0769, 5.698, 4.6538),
(3833, 'Simple Pleasures IV', 'Life, if we allow it to be, is chock-a-block full of simple pleasures. Your challenge is to show us one, to make us smile and say "Yeah, I''d like THAT!"', '2024-08-26', '2024-09-08', '2024-09-09', '2024-09-15', 29, 0, 648, 44, 5.87654, 6.8182, 5.81815, 4.7826),
(3834, 'People at Work II', 'In honor of Labor Day :-)', '2024-08-28', '2024-09-10', '2024-09-11', '2024-09-17', 23, 1, 583, 26, 5.98456, 7.5385, 5.94, 4.5),
(3835, 'Small Spaces', 'N/A', '2024-08-30', '2024-09-12', '2024-09-13', '2024-09-19', 20, 0, 463, 27, 5.78834, 6.7391, 5.7391, 4.7727),
(3836, 'Wide Open Spaces III', 'N/A', '2024-09-02', '2024-09-15', '2024-09-16', '2024-09-22', 24, 0, 575, 16, 6.14957, 7.6667, 5.9167, 5.0833),
(3837, 'Mid-Day Sun II', 'It''s the hardest time of day to make nice pictures outdoors, but you can use overhead sunlight to your advantage. Have a go at it!', '2024-09-04', '2024-09-17', '2024-09-18', '2024-09-24', 25, 0, 651, 21, 6.07066, 7.1923, 5.9437, 4.7308),
(3838, 'Free Study 2024-09', 'Free Study for September, 2024.', '2024-09-01', '2024-09-30', '2024-10-01', '2024-10-07', 43, 2, 1544, 108, 5.84391, 6.6389, 5.8919, 4.3056),
(3839, 'A Part of a Thing II', 'We can often find the heart or essence of a thing more in its parts or its details than in the whole. Go shoot with that in mind. This is not meant to be a "macro" challenge...', '2024-09-06', '2024-09-19', '2024-09-20', '2024-09-26', 29, 0, 712, 27, 5.84129, 6.6, 6.0, 4.0),
(3840, 'High Key VI', 'N/A', '2024-09-09', '2024-09-22', '2024-09-23', '2024-09-29', 17, 1, 357, 23, 5.61064, 6.7143, 5.5, 4.35),
(3841, 'Clouds IV', 'Clouds can contribute drama and impact to an image. They can be powerful and dominant, they can be ethereal and dreamlike, they can be foreboding or welcoming. Show us your best shot from this week in which clouds play a major role in the image.', '2024-09-11', '2024-09-24', '2024-09-25', '2024-10-01', 25, 0, 672, 22, 6.08036, 6.963, 6.09125, 5.2692),
(3842, 'Straight IV', 'Capture an image that includes only straight lines.', '2024-09-13', '2024-09-26', '2024-09-27', '2024-10-03', 21, 0, 553, 13, 6.03255, 6.9231, 6.0933, 4.6154),
