(3968, 'Contre-Jour VII', 'Contre-jour is a photographic term that means ''against the light'' and refers to pictures taken when the camera is pointing towards (or roughly towards) the main light source. Capture a photo using this technique.', '2024-12-25', '2025-01-07', '2025-01-08', '2025-01-14', 27, 0, 883, 14, 5.98075, 7.5152, 5.71235, 4.7419),
(3969, 'Centered Composition VIII', 'N/A', '2025-01-01', '2025-01-14', '2025-01-15', '2025-01-21', 32, 0, 1256, 31, 6.05732, 7.3333, 6.1026, 4.7692),
(3970, 'Grunge V', 'N/A', '2025-01-08', '2025-01-21', '2025-01-22', '2025-01-28', 24, 0, 799, 16, 5.71715, 6.6364, 5.6061, 4.4375),
(3971, 'Diagonal IV', 'Most of us tend to default to compositions that are oriented around strong horizontal or vertical axes. Your challenge this week is to incorporate a diagonal axis as the major compositional thrust of your image. Note that this does NOT require the presence of a diagonal "line".', '2025-01-15', '2025-01-28', '2025-01-29', '2025-02-04', 30, 0, 973, 35, 5.82631, 7.1818, 5.75, 4.5882),
(3972, 'Patterns in Nature II', 'N/A', '2025-01-22', '2025-02-04', '2025-02-05', '2025-02-11', 27, 0, 606, 24, 5.92574, 7.1364, 5.8636, 4.9565),
(3973, 'Negative Space XI', 'Use the space surrounding (and distinct from) your subject to create the WOW of the photograph.', '2025-01-29', '2025-02-11', '2025-02-12', '2025-02-18', 29, 1, 1107, 40, 6.06143, 7.0769, 5.96055, 4.8684),
(3974, 'Deep DOF V', 'Take control of your aperture this week and photograph a scene where everything is in focus.', '2025-02-05', '2025-02-18', '2025-02-19', '2025-02-25', 19, 0, 592, 44, 6.20777, 7.8333, 6.20615, 4.8125),
(3975, 'Simplicity III', 'Clarity of expression; lack of sophistication; absence of complexity; plainness. Capture the essence of simplicity in your photograph.', '2025-02-12', '2025-02-25', '2025-02-26', '2025-03-04', 38, 0, 1144, 31, 5.81381, 7.0667, 5.7419, 4.4483),
(3976, 'Bokeh XIII', 'Loosely defined, bokeh is the quality and "feel" of the out-of-focus foreground or background elements of a photo. It isn''t very interesting by itself, but take a photograph whose subject is enhanced by the bokeh in the image.', '2025-02-19', '2025-03-04', '2025-03-05', '2025-03-11', 28, 0, 810, 44, 6.02222, 7.5357, 6.0714, 4.1034),
(3977, 'Symmetry X', 'Close your eyes, bring your various parts into harmony, take a deep breath, then rise up and go seek the symmetry that abounds in our world.', '2025-02-26', '2025-03-11', '2025-03-12', '2025-03-18', 25, 0, 767, 13, 5.87875, 7.3871, 5.95, 4.2667),
(3978, 'Fill the Frame VIII', 'Compose your photograph so that nothing but your subject is in the frame.', '2025-03-05', '2025-03-18', '2025-03-19', '2025-03-25', 26, 0, 647, 19, 5.97682, 7.3077, 6.0, 4.52),
(3979, 'Painterly Photo III', 'Create a photo that resembles a painting or has a painterly feel to it.', '2025-03-12', '2025-03-25', '2025-03-26', '2025-04-01', 30, 0, 947, 49, 6.0528, 7.4688, 6.0323, 4.9063),
(3980, 'Framing VII', '"Frame" your subject, or your scene, on at least 2 sides by foreground or/and background objects. It''s NOT about "picture frames" or other artificial solutions, it''s about using existing elements to isolate and accentuate your subject.', '2025-03-19', '2025-04-01', '2025-04-02', '2025-04-08', 27, 0, 789, 17, 5.86565, 7.2414, 5.70835, 4.4138),
(3981, 'Rule of Odds', 'Use an odd number of subjects in a photo to create a more visually appealing and balanced image.', '2025-03-26', '2025-04-08', '2025-04-09', '2025-04-15', 27, 0, 788, 52, 5.84645, 7.2759, 5.79655, 4.2069),
(3982, 'Patterns VIII', 'Patterns are found everywhere. Find a pattern that captures your attention and hopefully ours as well.', '2025-04-02', '2025-04-15', '2025-04-16', '2025-04-22', 27, 0, 675, 21, 5.93926, 7.0435, 5.94155, 4.8),
(3983, 'High Key VII', 'A high key photograph is one where the overwhelming majority of the tones in the image are above middle gray (including any shadows) yet still maintains detail even in the brightest areas of the subject. Photograph a shot that''s high key this week.', '2025-04-09', '2025-04-22', '2025-04-23', '2025-04-29', 26, 0, 865, 44, 5.97225, 7.0303, 5.9697, 4.9091),
(3984, 'Juxtaposition IV', 'Juxtaposition is a powerful technique in photography, which essence is to place contrasting elements in the same frame and tell the viewer their story. The juxtaposition in your photography can combine such contrasting things as new and old, man-made and industrial, light and dark, or two different emotions.', '2025-04-16', '2025-04-29', '2025-04-30', '2025-05-06', 24, 0, 702, 34, 5.84046, 7.3448, 5.6897, 5.0345),
(3985, 'Backlighting VII', 'Shining light at an object from behind, or lighting areas behind the object you want to highlight. You can photograph anything you want, but the use of backlighting to enhance the photo is key. This is NOT a silhouette challenge, that''s a different technique.', '2025-04-23', '2025-05-06', '2025-05-07', '2025-05-13', 23, 1, 700, 47, 5.79143, 7.5161, 5.72095, 4.7419),
(3986, 'Balance V', 'Arrange the main subject and other elements within the frame of a photograph so that everything in the image has equal visual weight.', '2025-04-30', '2025-05-13', '2025-05-14', '2025-05-20', 25, 0, 761, 70, 6.03548, 7.0968, 6.01665, 4.9333),
(3987, 'In The Style Of: Bear_Music', 'Robert is ''retiring'' from his administrative duties here at DPChallenge. Help us send him off in style. Check out Bear_Music/Robert''s portfolio. He''s only entered 2,737 challenges! :-) Consider his various styles and submit an entry that honors his work.', '2025-05-07', '2025-05-20', '2025-05-21', '2025-05-27', 35, 0, 954, 49, 5.95493, 7.3077, 5.88675, 4.8846),
(3988, 'Foreground Interest', 'Place interesting elements in the front of a photo to draw the viewer''s eye in and create a sense of depth.', '2025-05-14', '2025-05-27', '2025-05-28', '2025-06-03', 28, 1, 936, 40, 5.80128, 7.1176, 5.697, 4.4516),
(3989, 'Subject Isolation', 'Draw the viewer''s attention to the main subject of an image by separating it from the background.', '2025-05-21', '2025-06-03', '2025-06-04', '2025-06-10', 28, 1, 824, 64, 5.91019, 7.1034, 5.8667, 4.6207),
(3990, 'Perspective XI', 'Use perspective to create a dramatic effect with your photograph.', '2025-05-28', '2025-06-10', '2025-06-11', '2025-06-17', 27, 0, 814, 38, 5.95577, 7.2, 5.7638, 4.7419),
(3991, 'Motion Panning VI', 'In still photography, motion panning is a technique used mostly to freeze a moving object whilst allowing motion blur in the (stationary) background. The desired result is usually a well-depicted, sharp subject in an almost impressionistic sea of blurred lines and colors.', '2025-06-04', '2025-06-17', '2025-06-18', '2025-06-24', 15, 1, 423, 19, 6.08747, 8.037, 6.10345, 4.8571),
(3992, 'Complementary Colors IX', 'Use two complementary colors to compose your photograph. For those of you who need a refresher, your main sets of complementary colors are red/green, blue/orange, yellow/purple.', '2025-06-11', '2025-06-24', '2025-06-25', '2025-07-01', 30, 0, 756, 54, 5.89021, 7.0769, 5.8, 4.7083),
(3993, 'Rule of Space II', 'The rule of space in photography is simply the act of adding visual space in front of the direction that an object is moving, looking, or pointing, to imply motion and direction and to lead the eye of the viewer.', '2025-06-18', '2025-07-01', '2025-07-02', '2025-07-08', 26, 0, 631, 63, 5.9683, 7.2917, 5.8333, 4.9615),
(3994, 'Rule of Thirds XI', 'The rule of thirds suggests that if you picture imaginary lines dividing your photograph in thirds (horizontally and vertically), your points of interest should be placed on the intersections of those lines. Your challenge is to take an interesting photograph using this technique.', '2025-06-25', '2025-07-08', '2025-07-09', '2025-07-15', 27, 0, 868, 33, 5.95392, 7.5, 5.89065, 4.9394),
(3995, 'Hidden Gem VIII (ARCHIVAL)', 'Dig through your archives to show us the best photo you''ve taken with a digital camera that you haven''t already entered in a challenge. Make sure you still have the original with valid EXIF in case it''s needed for validation.', '2025-07-02', '2025-07-15', '2025-07-16', '2025-07-22', 36, 0, 1126, 89, 6.1119, 7.0645, 5.9355, 5.2581),
(3996, 'Shallow DOF XIII', 'Shallow depth of field is often used to isolate a subject from its surrounding environment or to make it stand out. Find a creative use of a shallow depth of field for this week''s challenge.', '2025-07-09', '2025-07-22', '2025-07-23', '2025-07-29', 32, 0, 1095, 123, 5.9653, 7.2647, 5.8824, 4.6857),
(3997, 'Golden Ratio V', 'Use the Golden Ratio to inform the composition of your image. Learn about the Golden Ratio here.', '2025-07-16', '2025-07-29', '2025-07-30', '2025-08-05', 28, 1, 1014, 43, 5.81755, 7.1622, 5.8056, 4.6486),
(3998, 'Centered Composition IX', 'N/A', '2025-07-23', '2025-08-05', '2025-08-06', '2025-08-12', 39, 0, 1608, 87, 5.95896, 7.2857, 5.8875, 4.9),
(3999, 'Grunge VI', 'N/A', '2025-07-30', '2025-08-12', '2025-08-13', '2025-08-19', 30, 0, 1384, 98, 5.87934, 6.6957, 5.8298, 4.8444),
(4000, 'Unusual Crop (DPL6-1B)', 'N/A', '2025-08-06', '2025-08-19', '2025-08-20', '2025-08-26', 86, 0, 5574, 203, 5.67869, 6.9394, 5.6567, 4.4925),
(4001, 'Repetition II (DPL6-2B)', 'For this challenge, your photograph should include a repeating element or theme.', '2025-08-13', '2025-08-26', '2025-08-27', '2025-09-02', 76, 2, 4519, 134, 5.73379, 6.7377, 5.7241, 4.5806),
(4002, 'Negative Space XII (DPL6-3B)', 'Use the space surrounding (and distinct from) your subject to create the WOW of the photograph.', '2025-08-20', '2025-09-02', '2025-09-03', '2025-09-09', 83, 0, 4723, 114, 5.73301, 7.3158, 5.7233, 4.3559),
(4003, 'Bold (DPL6-4B)', 'N/A', '2025-08-27', '2025-09-09', '2025-09-10', '2025-09-16', 69, 0, 4197, 119, 5.78223, 7.5574, 5.7338, 4.6833),
(4004, 'Silhouettes XII (DPL6-5B)', 'N/A', '2025-09-03', '2025-09-16', '2025-09-17', '2025-09-23', 61, 1, 3451, 172, 5.80267, 7.0, 5.76085, 4.3448),
(4005, 'Mysterious II', 'N/A', '2025-09-10', '2025-09-23', '2025-09-24', '2025-09-30', 33, 1, 1292, 73, 5.83746, 7.0769, 5.78495, 4.6154),
(4006, 'Color - Pick One', 'Red, Blue, Yellow, Green, etc. Pick a color and present an image that the viewer will have no doubt as to the color you chose.', '2025-09-17', '2025-09-30', '2025-10-01', '2025-10-07', 30, 1, 1068, 72, 5.82865, 6.8571, 5.8571, 4.9706),
(4007, 'Leading Lines XIII', 'In photography, leading lines are used to draw the viewer into (or occasionally even out of) your photograph. Google the topic, then practice what you learned :-)', '2025-09-24', '2025-10-07', '2025-10-08', '2025-10-14', 31, 0, 1354, 84, 5.92245, 7.2093, 5.9429, 4.3864),
(4008, 'Lines & Circles III (DPL6-Playoff1B)', 'N/A', '2025-10-01', '2025-10-14', '2025-10-15', '2025-10-21', 56, 1, 2337, 163, 5.80787, 7.439, 5.6585, 4.3415),
(4009, 'Peaceful', 'N/A', '2025-10-08', '2025-10-21', '2025-10-22', '2025-10-28', 34, 1, 1519, 93, 6.00593, 7.1957, 5.9778, 4.5),
(4010, 'High Contrast XI (DPL6-Playoff2B)', 'Use high contrast to create impact in your photograph.', '2025-10-15', '2025-10-28', '2025-10-29', '2025-11-04', 58, 1, 2616, 163, 5.95757, 7.4043, 5.96, 4.7292),
(4011, 'Tools III', 'N/A', '2025-10-22', '2025-11-04', '2025-11-05', '2025-11-11', 20, 0, 706, 64, 5.79178, 6.8333, 5.7714, 4.3714),
(4012, 'Duotones VIII (DPL6-Playoff3B)', 'Your submission should only consist of two tones (black/white, sepia, etc).', '2025-10-29', '2025-11-11', '2025-11-12', '2025-11-18', 51, 1, 2330, 182, 5.92918, 7.1818, 5.8866, 4.7959),
(4013, 'Juxtaposition V', 'Juxtaposition is a powerful technique in photography, which essence is to place contrasting elements in the same frame and tell the viewer their story. The juxtaposition in your photography can combine such contrasting things as new and old, man-made and industrial, light and dark, or two different emotions.', '2025-11-05', '2025-11-18', '2025-11-19', '2025-11-25', 27, 0, 988, 31, 5.90891, 7.0278, 6.01315, 4.8919),
(4014, 'Backlighting VIII', 'Shining light at an object from behind, or lighting areas behind the object you want to highlight. You can photograph anything you want, but the use of backlighting to enhance the photo is key. This is NOT a silhouette challenge, that''s a different technique.', '2025-11-12', '2025-11-25', '2025-11-26', '2025-12-02', 30, 0, 842, 56, 5.90618, 7.2414, 5.6429, 4.6552),
(4015, 'Balance VI', 'Arrange the main subject and other elements within the frame of a photograph so that everything in the image has equal visual weight.', '2025-11-19', '2025-12-02', '2025-12-03', '2025-12-09', 26, 0, 857, 33, 5.83081, 6.9091, 5.7059, 4.7353),
(4016, 'Inanimate Macro III', 'We do lots of macro challenges, and the bugs seem to win ''em all. So NO bugs! NO animals! NO flowers, NO ferns! NO THING ALIVE! Rocks, glass, sand, metal, plastic, OBJECTS is the ticket here. Explore the inanimate world up close and personal.', '2025-11-26', '2025-12-09', '2025-12-10', '2025-12-16', 28, 0, 907, 42, 5.93054, 7.125, 5.9375, 4.8788),
(4017, 'Motion II', 'N/A', '2025-12-03', '2025-12-16', '2025-12-17', '2025-12-23', 23, 3, 765, 56, 5.88105, 7.2059, 5.83335, 4.7273),
(4018, 'Symmetry in Nature II', 'N/A', '2025-12-10', '2025-12-23', '2025-12-24', '2025-12-30', 22, 0, 731, 49, 5.86594, 7.6364, 5.7941, 4.7059),
(4019, 'Edges IV', 'N/A', '2025-12-24', '2026-01-06', '2026-01-07', '2026-01-13', 33, 0, 1286, 67, 6.07543, 7.2308, 6.0128, 5.1282),
(4020, 'Contre-Jour VIII', 'Contre-jour is a photographic term that means ''against the light'' and refers to pictures taken when the camera is pointing towards (or roughly towards) the main light source. Capture a photo using this technique.', '2026-04-08', '2026-04-21', '2026-04-22', '2026-04-28', 33, 0, 1061, 86, 6.00471, 7.4063, 5.88855, 5.1333),
(4021, 'Billboard III', 'Take a photograph that might grace a highway billboard (those large signs you see on the side of the road). Your submission should be in landscape orientation, and should be twice as wide as it is tall to simulate a common billboard aspect ratio. Title your entry with what the billboard would be promoting.', '2026-01-07', '2026-01-20', '2026-01-21', '2026-01-27', 20, 0, 552, 25, 6.06884, 6.9643, 6.0357, 3.8889),
(4022, 'All I Want for Christmas III', 'Create a photographic representation of what YOU want for Christmas (or your next Birthday, if you don''t celebrate Christmas).', '2024-12-06', '2024-12-19', '2024-12-20', '2024-12-26', 11, 0, 159, 11, 5.91824, 7.2143, 5.7262, 5.0),
(4023, 'Alone in a Crowd II', 'Create a photo in which someone or something is clearly on its own in a crowded situation.', '2024-12-13', '2024-12-26', '2024-12-27', '2025-01-02', 11, 0, 364, 42, 6.0989, 6.8182, 6.1998, 5.0909),
(4024, 'Animals (no People) in B&W', 'Capture an animal photo (no people please) and present it in B&W.', '2024-12-20', '2025-01-02', '2025-01-03', '2025-01-09', 26, 0, 763, 94, 6.14941, 7.4828, 6.1034, 5.2069),
(4025, 'Backsides II', 'Everything that has a front side, by definition, has a back side. Your challenge this week is to get behind your subject, as it were, and show us the side less seen.', '2024-12-27', '2025-01-09', '2025-01-10', '2025-01-16', 26, 0, 760, 30, 6.125, 7.6897, 6.0667, 5.2667),
(4026, 'Best of 2024', 'Now''s the chance to show us that special image you held back from us all year so you could wow us at the start of 2025.', '2025-01-03', '2025-01-16', '2025-01-17', '2025-01-23', 48, 0, 1502, 56, 6.11318, 7.2813, 6.1613, 4.9355),
(4027, 'Barns, Farms or Rural Countrysides IV', 'N/A', '2025-01-10', '2025-01-23', '2025-01-24', '2025-01-30', 16, 0, 453, 13, 6.13245, 7.2857, 6.2414, 4.6897),
(4028, 'Chains II', 'Take a photo of some kind of chain. The chain could be physical or mental or emotional, real or symbolic.', '2025-01-17', '2025-01-30', '2025-01-31', '2025-02-06', 22, 1, 687, 35, 5.79185, 7.1613, 5.7097, 4.5484),
(4029, 'Chalk II', 'Chalk is colorful, fun, and can be used in many creative ways. Take a picture either portraying or using chalk.', '2025-01-24', '2025-02-06', '2025-02-07', '2025-02-13', 13, 0, 327, 5, 6.26911, 7.0, 6.38, 5.44),
(4030, 'Dappled Light III', 'One of the most challenging lighting situations include dappled light. Create a photo that has dappled light as its main light source.', '2025-01-31', '2025-02-13', '2025-02-14', '2025-02-20', 19, 0, 549, 15, 5.91439, 7.3214, 5.8655, 4.6207),
(4031, 'Chocolate II', 'White, dark, milk, melted, solid... chocolate comes in many forms and shades. Compose a photograph using chocolate as your main subject of focus.', '2025-02-07', '2025-02-20', '2025-02-21', '2025-02-27', 17, 0, 425, 29, 5.89882, 7.375, 5.74, 4.76),
(4032, 'Deja Vu VI', 'Choose a previous ribbon-winning entry THAT ISN''T YOUR OWN and try to emulate it as closely as possible!', '2025-02-14', '2025-02-27', '2025-02-28', '2025-03-06', 14, 0, 351, 34, 6.63533, 7.44, 6.6, 5.3077),
(4034, 'Why II', 'Why is this a good idea? Why didn''t I think of that? Why not? Why ask why?', '2025-02-28', '2025-03-13', '2025-03-14', '2025-03-20', 25, 0, 535, 9, 5.89907, 6.8095, 5.8593, 5.1429),
(4035, 'Fairy Tales IV', 'Create a photograph that depicts a fairy tale or evokes a fairy tale quality.', '2025-03-07', '2025-03-20', '2025-03-21', '2025-03-27', 14, 0, 307, 27, 5.76547, 7.4545, 5.7273, 5.0),
(4036, 'Feathers II', 'On or off a bird, close up or not, but keeping feathers as the focal point - make it exciting under standard editing rules.', '2025-03-14', '2025-03-27', '2025-03-28', '2025-04-03', 21, 0, 563, 42, 6.24156, 8.1923, 6.2258, 5.0),
(4037, 'Games IV', 'N/A', '2025-03-21', '2025-04-03', '2025-04-04', '2025-04-10', 16, 1, 421, 33, 5.83373, 6.7692, 5.7143, 5.0),
(4038, 'Garbage IV', 'Turn garbage into art this week by taking an appealing photo of a generally not-so-appealing subject.', '2025-03-28', '2025-04-10', '2025-04-11', '2025-04-17', 18, 0, 401, 39, 5.71072, 6.5, 5.7727, 4.8182),
(4039, 'Glimpse III', 'Something seen fleetingly, partially or vaguely.', '2025-04-04', '2025-04-17', '2025-04-18', '2025-04-24', 22, 0, 455, 18, 5.97582, 7.3333, 5.7895, 4.7619),
(4040, 'Hidden Faces II', 'Photograph a face "hidden" in the world around you. Look for objects that clearly could be viewed as eyes, nose and mouth. The face you submit may not be something that is intended to be a face (that is, not a person, animal, insect, toy or anything else that has a "face").', '2025-04-11', '2025-04-24', '2025-04-25', '2025-05-01', 13, 0, 367, 32, 5.88283, 7.1786, 5.86145, 4.8148),
(4041, 'Birds in Flight II', 'Photograph one or more birds in flight.', '2025-04-18', '2025-05-01', '2025-05-02', '2025-05-08', 17, 1, 443, 74, 6.3228, 7.52, 6.24505, 4.92),
(4042, 'In the Rain II (ARCHIVAL)', 'Take a photo where your subject is in the rain.', '2025-04-25', '2025-05-08', '2025-05-09', '2025-05-15', 27, 0, 735, 64, 6.21633, 7.6667, 6.05555, 5.3333),
(4043, 'Light and Shadow II', 'Light is a requirement for photography, but where there is light there is shadow. Capture an image where both of these elements play an important role -- an image where light and shadow seem to vie for attention.', '2025-05-02', '2025-05-15', '2025-05-16', '2025-05-22', 26, 0, 765, 66, 5.94902, 6.8966, 5.9333, 5.0),
(4044, 'Magnifying Glass II', 'Use a magnifying glass in some creative way.', '2025-05-09', '2025-05-22', '2025-05-23', '2025-05-29', 19, 0, 403, 21, 5.98015, 7.1818, 5.9024, 5.0);
INSERT INTO challenges ("id", "name", "description", "submission_start", "submission_end", "voting_start", "voting_end", "num_submissions", "num_disqualifications", "num_votes", "num_comments", "average_score", "highest_score", "median_score", "lowest_score") VALUES
(4045, 'Postage Stamp III', 'Mail is so old, it''s time to pay homage. Pick a country, take a photo, engage your design aesthetic. Show us an original design for a postage stamp.', '2025-05-16', '2025-05-29', '2025-05-30', '2025-06-05', 17, 0, 543, 47, 6.28729, 7.5, 6.41595, 5.1515),
(4046, 'Negative Image V', 'Capture an image that works well when inverted, via post processing, into a negative.', '2025-05-23', '2025-06-05', '2025-06-06', '2025-06-12', 35, 0, 1075, 62, 5.97767, 7.0909, 5.98385, 4.8333),
(4047, 'Odd III', 'Find a creative way to photograph the concept of "odd".', '2025-05-30', '2025-06-12', '2025-06-13', '2025-06-19', 24, 0, 747, 32, 5.76305, 6.7742, 5.7188, 4.625),
(4048, 'On the Road IV', 'Shoot from a moving car, bus, or train. Some portion of your vehicle, the road, or the tracks should be in your image.', '2025-06-06', '2025-06-19', '2025-06-20', '2025-06-26', 20, 0, 521, 20, 6.00192, 6.9615, 5.8846, 5.1481),
(4049, 'Seed III', '"Seed" has a lot of potential meanings; fertilize your imagination for this one, and show us the essence of "seed" your way.', '2025-06-13', '2025-06-26', '2025-06-27', '2025-07-03', 22, 1, 540, 23, 5.82037, 7.0, 5.75, 5.0),
(4050, 'Shapes VIII', 'N/A', '2025-06-20', '2025-07-03', '2025-07-04', '2025-07-10', 22, 0, 512, 51, 5.93359, 7.8261, 5.7826, 4.9565),
(4051, 'Motivational Poster V', 'As seen in many offices/work places. Your title should be the motivational phrase.', '2025-06-27', '2025-07-10', '2025-07-11', '2025-07-17', 20, 0, 661, 61, 5.96823, 7.0606, 5.7353, 4.5152),
(4052, 'Biology II', 'Show us your best interpretation of the science of Biology.', '2025-07-04', '2025-07-17', '2025-07-18', '2025-07-24', 17, 0, 434, 33, 6.19124, 7.0769, 6.2311, 4.72),
(4053, 'In the Garden III', 'Simple enough -- compose a photograph somehow related to the garden. Here''s the catch... the main subject of your photograph may NOT be a flower.', '2025-07-11', '2025-07-24', '2025-07-25', '2025-07-31', 30, 0, 953, 72, 5.75656, 6.871, 5.7188, 3.9355),
(4054, 'In the Marketplace II', 'N/A', '2025-07-18', '2025-07-31', '2025-08-01', '2025-08-07', 17, 0, 524, 16, 5.7729, 6.5484, 5.8009, 4.7742),
(4055, 'Lens Effect III', 'This is a minimal editing challenge where the entry should demonstrate some interesting lens effects... this could cover specialist lenses such as Lensbaby as well as techniques such as free lensing... the aim of the challenge and minimal editing rule is to see what can be achieved straight from the camera without post-processing distortions...', '2025-07-25', '2025-08-07', '2025-08-08', '2025-08-14', 21, 1, 656, 65, 5.8247, 7.1613, 5.8095, 4.871),
(4056, 'Indulgence II', 'Indulge yourself this week by photographing an unnecessary luxury. Excess is the name of the game!', '2025-08-01', '2025-08-14', '2025-08-15', '2025-08-21', 16, 1, 556, 32, 5.84532, 6.6667, 5.7353, 4.4118),
(4057, 'Action V', 'Take a photo that captures action or a sense of action.', '2025-08-08', '2025-08-21', '2025-08-22', '2025-08-28', 31, 2, 1217, 91, 6.09942, 7.5, 5.92495, 5.0513),
(4058, 'Infinite III', 'Photograph something seemingly infinite.', '2025-08-15', '2025-08-28', '2025-08-29', '2025-09-04', 23, 1, 851, 64, 5.68978, 7.2162, 5.65325, 4.5405),
(4059, 'Album Cover II', 'Create an album cover for a real or fictitious band.', '2025-08-22', '2025-09-04', '2025-09-05', '2025-09-11', 25, 0, 900, 53, 6.06111, 7.3056, 6.05635, 5.1667),
(4060, 'Batteries II', 'Your photo should include 1 or more batteries.', '2025-08-29', '2025-09-11', '2025-09-12', '2025-09-18', 18, 0, 702, 57, 6.01567, 8.025, 5.8718, 4.8947),
(4061, 'Benches III', 'Include 1 or more benches (the kind you sit on) in your composition.', '2025-09-05', '2025-09-18', '2025-09-19', '2025-09-25', 26, 0, 917, 32, 5.8626, 6.8056, 5.75, 5.0857),
(4062, 'Miniature IV', 'N/A', '2025-09-12', '2025-09-25', '2025-09-26', '2025-10-02', 22, 1, 656, 22, 5.97561, 6.5667, 5.9333, 5.1667),
(4063, 'Reflections in Water III', 'N/A', '2025-09-19', '2025-10-02', '2025-10-03', '2025-10-09', 22, 0, 674, 25, 6.0089, 7.4194, 5.7419, 5.2),
(4064, 'Freedom IV', 'Create a photograph that communicates the concept of "freedom," but do so without using flags or other national symbols in your final image.', '2025-09-26', '2025-10-09', '2025-10-10', '2025-10-16', 22, 0, 799, 36, 5.9199, 7.25, 5.7105, 4.8611),
(4065, 'Bored III', 'Try not to bore your audience, but depict boredom in your photo.', '2025-10-03', '2025-10-16', '2025-10-17', '2025-10-23', 21, 0, 697, 36, 5.82353, 7.1818, 5.7313, 5.0909),
(4066, 'Ansel Adams VI', 'Take a photograph in the style of this famous black & white photographer.', '2025-10-10', '2025-10-23', '2025-10-24', '2025-10-30', 20, 0, 725, 34, 6.10759, 7.6111, 5.8919, 5.2222),
(4067, 'At Rest II', 'Your subject should be placed, seated, or lying stably, with a feeling of calm to the shot.', '2025-10-17', '2025-10-30', '2025-10-31', '2025-11-06', 25, 0, 877, 55, 5.91904, 7.1176, 5.88235, 4.7568),
(4068, 'Hidden Gem 4,000 (ARCHIVAL)', 'It''s time to celebrate! DPC''s 4,000th challenge! Enter one of your favorite photos that we haven''t seen yet. This is an Archival challenge so dig into your old libraries, but don''t forget we still need valid EXIF data. :-)', '2025-10-24', '2025-11-06', '2025-11-07', '2025-11-13', 51, 2, 2049, 217, 6.25525, 7.7073, 6.19725, 4.7368),
(4069, 'Cemetery II', 'Tread lightly this week as you take your best picture of this challenge topic.', '2025-10-31', '2025-11-13', '2025-11-14', '2025-11-20', 17, 0, 611, 31, 6.14566, 7.0, 6.1115, 4.8333),
(4070, 'Fog & Mist II (ARCHIVAL)', 'If you''ve ever shot fog or mist, now''s the time to break ''em out.', '2025-11-07', '2025-11-20', '2025-11-21', '2025-11-27', 43, 0, 1500, 66, 6.20333, 7.6571, 6.24425, 4.5429),
(4071, 'Authority II', 'Authority of some sort exists everywhere you look. Rules and regulations are everywhere. Photograph a great example of authority.', '2025-11-14', '2025-11-27', '2025-11-28', '2025-12-04', 14, 0, 410, 31, 5.5, 6.931, 5.3448, 4.3667),
(4072, 'Postcard V', 'Put together a worthy postcard! Extended editing. Have fun!', '2025-11-21', '2025-12-04', '2025-12-05', '2025-12-11', 18, 1, 610, 42, 6.01967, 7.2121, 6.0882, 4.7059),
