(4080, 'Best of 2025', 'Now''s the chance to show us that special image you held back from us all year so you could wow us at the start of 2026.', '2026-01-05', '2026-01-18', '2026-01-19', '2026-01-25', 50, 0, 2096, 93, 6.18655, 7.4524, 6.1905, 4.5366),
(4081, 'Lost', 'N/A', '2026-01-12', '2026-01-25', '2026-01-26', '2026-02-01', 17, 1, 544, 27, 5.85478, 7.0, 5.82815, 5.0303),
(4082, 'Time Capsules', 'Brief: Capture something tied to a specific era. Tips: Seek retro or fading traditions. Examples: Old phones, vintage cars, classic clothing.', '2026-01-19', '2026-02-01', '2026-02-02', '2026-02-08', 15, 0, 335, 7, 6.01194, 7.6818, 6.06525, 4.7273),
(4083, 'Hobby (other than photography) II', 'Show us what you do for a hobby, the "fruits" of your hobby as it were. Photography is specifically excluded here since we ALL do that :-) This one''s for the weavers, the modelers, the painters, the bakers, the gardeners, etc :-)', '2026-01-26', '2026-02-08', '2026-02-09', '2026-02-15', 26, 0, 701, 38, 6.20827, 7.2222, 6.0714, 5.48),
(4084, 'Square Crop VII', 'N/A', '2025-12-31', '2026-01-13', '2026-01-14', '2026-01-20', 42, 1, 1590, 78, 6.11069, 7.2368, 6.1053, 4.7368),
(4085, 'Foreground Interest II', 'Place interesting elements in the front of a photo to draw the viewer''s eye in and create a sense of depth.', '2026-01-14', '2026-01-27', '2026-01-28', '2026-02-03', 31, 1, 972, 81, 5.88374, 7.4839, 5.72885, 4.8065),
(4086, 'Still-Life Triptych', 'Create one still life and then photograph it three different ways by keeping the point of view the same, but changing the lighting each time. Create a triptych of your final results.', '2026-01-21', '2026-02-03', '2026-02-04', '2026-02-10', 13, 0, 278, 18, 6.24101, 7.0909, 6.2554, 5.0455),
(4087, 'OOF', 'Present an intentionally out of focus image that is pleasing to the eye.', '2026-01-28', '2026-02-10', '2026-02-11', '2026-02-17', 25, 0, 980, 38, 5.67959, 7.0769, 5.6705, 4.4),
(4088, 'Acronyms II', 'An acronym is a word created from the initials of words in a phrase, such as RAM (Random Access Memory) or DPC (Digital Photography Challenge). Title your image with your chosen acronym, and let your image explain what the letters represent!', '2026-01-09', '2026-01-22', '2026-01-23', '2026-01-29', 20, 0, 539, 54, 5.89054, 7.037, 5.8077, 5.0),
(4089, 'Faces of Emotion (ARCHIVAL)', 'Brief: Highlight raw human expressions. Tips: Seek candid laughter, surprise, or sadness. Examples: Audience reactions, candid portraits, joyful celebrations.', '2025-12-26', '2026-01-08', '2026-01-09', '2026-01-15', 31, 1, 1055, 63, 6.08436, 7.2353, 6.0147, 5.0286),
(4090, 'Hidden Corners', 'Brief: Reveal overlooked spaces. Tips: Explore alleys, stairwells, or abandoned spots. Examples: Graffiti walls, forgotten benches, shadowy corridors.', '2026-01-23', '2026-02-05', '2026-02-06', '2026-02-12', 22, 0, 635, 16, 5.91811, 6.9667, 5.7931, 4.9643),
(4091, 'Words III', 'Take a photograph where complete words -- not just individual letters -- play a creative role in your composition.', '2026-02-06', '2026-02-19', '2026-02-20', '2026-02-26', 23, 0, 577, 35, 5.84402, 7.3077, 5.8231, 4.64),
(4092, 'Trees XI', 'N/A', '2026-01-02', '2026-01-15', '2026-01-16', '2026-01-22', 27, 0, 941, 59, 5.97024, 7.0, 6.0, 4.8529),
(4093, 'Toy Photography II', 'N/A', '2026-01-16', '2026-01-29', '2026-01-30', '2026-02-05', 27, 0, 785, 25, 5.73631, 6.6923, 5.74135, 4.6897),
(4094, 'Conceptual Photography', 'Draw upon the imagination to create an image that is visually striking and thought-provoking. Tip: Google "Conceptual Photography" for some great ideas!', '2026-01-30', '2026-02-12', '2026-02-13', '2026-02-19', 17, 0, 575, 37, 6.08, 7.6, 6.13605, 4.4545),
(4095, 'Cubism II', 'Cubism was a 20th-century avant-garde artistic movement that revolutionized the art world. Painters such as Pablo Picasso, Fernand Léger, Georges Braque and Juan Gris embraced this new artistic sensibility. Create your own cubist photograph.', '2026-04-06', '2026-04-20', '2026-04-21', '2026-04-27', 23, 1, 804, 76, 5.90796, 7.0909, 5.783, 4.8824),
(4096, 'Stained', 'N/A', '2026-02-09', '2026-02-22', '2026-02-23', '2026-03-01', 19, 1, 591, 56, 5.86294, 7.3226, 5.71525, 4.9688),
(4097, 'Generations (ARCHIVAL)', 'Brief: Contrast age and time through portraits. Tips: Pair young and old subjects. Examples: Grandparent and child, old vs. new toys.', '2026-02-16', '2026-03-01', '2026-03-02', '2026-03-08', 24, 0, 561, 51, 6.03922, 7.7917, 5.9167, 4.75),
(4098, 'Curiosity II', 'N/A', '2026-02-23', '2026-03-08', '2026-03-09', '2026-03-15', 30, 0, 957, 49, 5.82341, 6.871, 5.7273, 5.0333),
(4099, 'Hidden Patterns', 'Brief: Discover repetition or geometry in unexpected places. Tips: Look for shadows, reflections, or textures. Examples: Fence lines, tiled floors, repeating shadows.', '2026-02-04', '2026-02-17', '2026-02-18', '2026-02-24', 24, 1, 659, 51, 5.84522, 7.2593, 5.6923, 4.8889),
(4100, 'Fill the Frame IX', 'Compose your photograph so that nothing but your subject is in the frame.', '2026-02-11', '2026-02-24', '2026-02-25', '2026-03-03', 37, 0, 1197, 63, 5.79114, 7.4848, 5.8485, 4.3333),
(4101, 'Bokeh XIV', 'Loosely defined, bokeh is the quality and "feel" of the out-of-focus foreground or background elements of a photo. It isn''t very interesting by itself, but take a photograph whose subject is enhanced by the bokeh in the image.', '2026-02-18', '2026-03-03', '2026-03-04', '2026-03-10', 27, 0, 1006, 22, 6.12425, 7.5385, 6.14445, 4.7838),
(4102, 'Wildlife X', 'For the purpose of this challenge, "wildlife" should be considered non-domesticated mammals, birds, reptiles and amphibians living in a natural environment.', '2026-02-25', '2026-03-10', '2026-03-11', '2026-03-17', 30, 0, 1109, 82, 6.08927, 7.3784, 6.1842, 4.027),
(4103, 'Mirrors IV', 'Photograph anything you want, but your photograph should include a mirror, the mirror should be evident in the photograph, and neither the photographer nor the camera being used should appear in the photo.', '2026-02-13', '2026-02-26', '2026-02-27', '2026-03-05', 21, 0, 600, 28, 5.90333, 7.2857, 5.8107, 4.8571),
(4104, 'Urban Geometry', 'Brief: Focus on shapes, lines, and symmetry in cityscapes. Tips: Use strong angles, reflections, or repeating structures. Examples: Bridges, staircases, skyscraper windows.', '2026-02-20', '2026-03-05', '2026-03-06', '2026-03-12', 25, 0, 677, 56, 6.05318, 7.4815, 6.01925, 4.8214),
