(4133, 'Motion Panning VII', 'In still photography, motion panning is a technique used mostly to freeze a moving object whilst allowing motion blur in the (stationary) background. The desired result is usually a well-depicted, sharp subject in an almost impressionistic sea of blurred lines and colors.', '2026-04-20', '2026-05-03', '2026-05-04', '2026-05-10', 17, 0, 481, 42, 6.14137, 7.931, 6.1607, 4.5172),
