(4161, 'Rule of Odds II', 'Use an odd number of subjects in a photo to create a visually appealing and balanced image.', '2026-06-05', '2026-06-18', '2026-06-19', '2026-06-25', 27, 0, 1110, 12, 5.8045, 7.6341, 5.59755, 4.9024),
(4162, 'Seeing the Unseen II', 'In the book The Little Prince, written by Antoine de Saint-Exupéry, there is a meaningful quote. “What is essential is invisible to the eye.” The most valuable things in life cannot be seen or touched, but can only be deeply felt. Show us what truly matters to you.', '2026-06-08', '2026-06-21', '2026-06-22', '2026-06-28', 30, 0, 1085, 32, 5.9576, 7.0833, 5.9459, 4.8611),
(4163, 'Music V', 'Create an image that sings of "music" in the viewer''s eye.', '2026-06-10', '2026-06-23', '2026-06-24', '2026-06-30', 25, 0, 979, 40, 5.87334, 7.0541, 5.68395, 4.525),
(4164, 'Shadows XII', 'Shift your focus from details to shapes. Look for scenes where light creates strong shadows—like the sun setting behind a person or bright daylight casting outlines on the ground. Let the shadows inform your image.', '2026-06-12', '2026-06-25', '2026-06-26', '2026-07-02', 27, 2, 1132, 71, 5.74293, 6.9524, 5.6786, 5.0),
(4165, 'Boxy Composition II', 'N/A', '2026-06-15', '2026-06-28', '2026-06-29', '2026-07-05', 33, 0, 1365, 73, 5.79267, 7.5122, 5.6629, 4.6279),
(4166, 'Vote out of the box Free Study', 'Challenge the "normal" aspect of your voting pattern and use the whole range offered (1 - 10). Nobody can check you, but do it anyway. Pick your 1s and 10s and see what happens in between. Commenting might help you think it through. And of course, in order for this to work and be fun, everyone needs to ENTER AND then VOTE!', '2026-06-17', '2026-06-30', '2026-07-01', '2026-07-07', 44, 0, 2026, 100, 5.56417, 7.6304, 5.4468, 3.4348),
(4167, 'Bold Colors', 'N/A', '2026-06-19', '2026-07-02', '2026-07-03', '2026-07-09', 28, 2, 1211, 84, 5.8109, 6.7556, 5.8372, 5.0714),
(4168, 'Square Crop VIII (DPL2026-1A)', 'N/A', '2026-06-22', '2026-07-05', '2026-07-06', '2026-07-12', 80, 0, 5151, 202, 5.85809, 7.2239, 5.8308, 4.625),
(4169, 'Unusual Point of View III (DPL2026-1B)', 'Show us your subject from an unusual or unexpected point of view.', '2026-06-24', '2026-07-07', '2026-07-08', '2026-07-14', 75, 1, 4278, 121, 5.75503, 6.8889, 5.78565, 4.4909),
(4170, 'Beatabg Tribute (Archival)', 'In honor of Beata Barbara Gilbert 1984 – 2026, an exceptional member of our community. With love from DPC. This challenge is open to all members and registered users.', '2026-06-26', '2026-07-09', '2026-07-10', '2026-07-16', 40, 0, 1817, 63, 6.29554, 7.2826, 6.1739, 5.3778),
(4171, 'Everyday Objects III (DPL2026-2A)', 'AKA: Finding Magic in the mundane. Take a common, everyday object that most anybody would recognize and use it as the focal point of an interesting photographic composition.', '2026-06-29', '2026-07-12', '2026-07-13', '2026-07-19', 76, 0, 4390, 111, 5.59886, 7.0, 5.6, 4.6842),
(4172, 'Free Study 2026-05', 'Free Study for May, 2026.', '2026-05-01', '2026-05-31', '2026-06-01', '2026-06-07', 39, 0, 809, 64, 6.08405, 7.381, 6.07035, 4.9048),
(4173, 'Circle VIII (DPL2026-2B)', 'Take a photograph where this basic shape is a key element (or elements) in your composition.', '2026-07-01', '2026-07-14', '2026-07-15', '2026-07-21', 80, 0, 4429, 152, 5.67013, 6.7091, 5.6923, 4.4444),
(4174, 'Black and White Still Life V', 'N/A', '2026-07-03', '2026-07-16', '2026-07-17', '2026-07-23', 31, 0, 1150, 86, 5.46174, 7.0541, 5.30655, 4.5135),
(4175, 'Composite V (DPL2026-3A)', 'Create a composite of two or more photos taken during the challenge period. Have fun.', '2026-07-06', '2026-07-19', '2026-07-20', '2026-07-26', 62, 0, 3322, 166, 5.9124, 7.8704, 5.8393, 4.8302),
(4176, 'Centered Composition X (DPL2026-3B)', 'N/A', '2026-07-08', '2026-07-21', '2026-07-22', '2026-07-28', 79, 0, 3998, 79, 5.7091, 7.0784, 5.76755, 3.8333),
(4177, 'Ugly to Lovely II', 'Take what most might consider "ugly" and make it "lovely" by the way you photograph it.', '2026-07-10', '2026-07-23', '2026-07-24', '2026-07-30', 24, 0, 803, 42, 5.81445, 6.7879, 5.7879, 4.7429),
(4178, 'Wide Angle VII', 'Go as wide as you can, and make it interesting.', '2026-07-13', '2026-07-26', '2026-07-27', '2026-08-02', 35, 0, 1452, 43, 5.9573, 7.439, 5.87775, 4.2683),
(4179, 'one-of-a-kind', 'Gina Rothfels was a long time devoted member of DPC. She had a unique way of looking at and seeing things. View her portfolio and take a photo in her honor. GinaRothfels', '2026-07-15', '2026-07-28', '2026-07-29', '2026-08-04', 35, 0, 1262, 11, 6.07607, 6.7143, 6.1082, 4.75),
(4180, 'Grey III', 'Capture the essence and subtlety of the color grey. There may be color in your image (this isn''t a B/W challenge) but there doesn''t have to be.', '2026-07-17', '2026-07-30', '2026-07-31', '2026-08-06', 32, 3, 1064, 45, 5.58929, 7.1212, 5.4706, 4.4545),
(4181, 'Body of Water V (DPL2026-4A)', 'Oceans, rivers, ponds, lakes, streams, brooks, fjords, swamps, waterfalls, dams, reservoirs, puddles, etc. Natural water takes on many shapes. Capture a naturally made body of water or even a man made one like a reservoir. No water drops, wine glasses or man made containers please.', '2026-07-20', '2026-08-02', '2026-08-03', '2026-08-09', 77, 1, 4588, 163, 5.77071, 7.2833, 5.73705, 4.4483),
(4182, 'Shutter Speed:One Tenth of a Second (DPL2026-4B)', 'One tenth of a second is just enough to turn motion into something beautiful. Freeze a hint of movement or let it whisper through your frame, and show us what happens in that fleeting slice of time.', '2026-07-22', '2026-08-04', '2026-08-05', '2026-08-11', 72, 0, 4345, 170, 5.59471, 6.8814, 5.623, 3.8),
(4183, 'Big', 'Photograph something Big. Or photograph something small and make it look Big. You decide.', '2026-07-24', '2026-08-06', '2026-08-07', '2026-08-13', 27, 0, 1016, 55, 5.85925, 6.7297, 6.0128, 4.6154),
(4184, 'Street Photography IX (DPL2026-5A)', 'Street photography records everyday life in a public place. It is most definitely not limited to a street. It may include candid pictures of strangers (but please be polite). Street photography can be documentary in style, fine art, abstract, or funny. It can be an observation or an interpretation of one. Get out and shoot. And please make it interesting.', '2026-07-27', '2026-08-09', '2026-08-10', '2026-08-16', 68, 0, 3511, 80, 5.62973, 6.6731, 5.5882, 4.6667),
(4185, 'Sepia IV (DPL2026-5B)', 'Create a photograph that uses an overall sepia tone effectively.', '2026-07-29', '2026-08-11', '2026-08-12', '2026-08-18', 78, 0, 4403, 170, 5.48081, 6.6667, 5.4912, 3.8545),
(4186, 'Group Portrait II', 'Include 3 or more human beings in your photograph.', '2026-07-31', '2026-08-13', '2026-08-14', '2026-08-20', 17, 0, 651, 11, 5.92319, 7.5, 5.7105, 4.7632),
(4187, 'Perspective XII', 'Use perspective to create a dramatic effect with your photograph.', '2026-08-03', '2026-08-16', '2026-08-17', '2026-08-23', 27, 0, 868, 61, 6.07373, 7.0909, 6.06365, 4.6452),
(4188, 'Bizarrechitechture V', 'Sometimes the built environment can smack you right between the eyes. Show us weird construction, show us bizarre engineering.', '2026-08-05', '2026-08-18', '2026-08-19', '2026-08-25', 22, 0, 817, 33, 6.06242, 7.4722, 6.0526, 4.5676),
(4189, 'Markets & Bazaars', 'Brief: Vibrant scenes of trade and exchange. Tips: Capture color, chaos, and human interaction. Examples: Farmers? markets, flea stalls, spice shops.', '2026-08-07', '2026-08-20', '2026-08-21', '2026-08-27', 20, 0, 664, 32, 5.69578, 6.5882, 5.6667, 4.9697),
(4190, 'Shapes in Black & White II', 'Henri Cartier-Bresson once said, "The rhythm of surfaces, lines, and values is for me the essence of photography; composition should be a constant of preoccupation... an organic coordination of visual elements." Capture this sentiment by encapsulating the elements that abstract into light, texture, shape, and shadow.', '2026-08-10', '2026-08-23', '2026-08-24', '2026-08-30', 37, 0, 1477, 91, 5.96682, 6.8, 5.93775, 4.75),
(4191, 'HDR XI', 'Use HDR (High Dynamic Range) exposure/processing techniques to expand the dynamic range of your image.', '2026-08-12', '2026-08-25', '2026-08-26', '2026-09-01', 25, 0, 906, 32, 6.13135, 7.6111, 6.13515, 4.6667),
(4192, 'Celebrations IV (ARCHIVAL)', 'Show us how you have documented joy and festivity at a special event and turned moments into magic.', '2026-08-14', '2026-08-27', '2026-08-28', '2026-09-03', 20, 1, 716, 24, 6.14525, 7.4722, 6.0278, 4.8571),
